1
00:01:20,243 --> 00:01:22,843
(AI technology was utilized
in the production of this program.)

2
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:31,276
(If no one chooses you,
the two-day date ends.)

3
00:01:34,043 --> 00:01:37,443
(The AI partners have
already made their choices.)

4
00:01:54,112 --> 00:01:56,112
Being chosen by them was shocking enough,

5
00:01:56,678 --> 00:01:58,577
but standing there
like that was just as shocking.

6
00:01:59,345 --> 00:02:01,787
Every moment was shocking.

7
00:02:01,912 --> 00:02:06,312
What if no one chooses him?

8
00:02:06,745 --> 00:02:10,077
Wouldn't it be embarrassing
if he got rejected?

9
00:02:10,078 --> 00:02:12,145
If he gets rejected, he dies, doesn't he?

10
00:02:13,378 --> 00:02:16,165
Not die, but it'd be humiliating.

11
00:02:16,166 --> 00:02:17,945
- I see.
- Right.

12
00:02:20,945 --> 00:02:24,377
(Da Hee, will you continue
the date with Kian84?)

13
00:02:24,378 --> 00:02:25,278
It's Da Hee first.

14
00:02:25,279 --> 00:02:26,812
Honestly, she was...

15
00:02:27,912 --> 00:02:31,011
(Da Hee left during their fishing date.)

16
00:02:31,012 --> 00:02:32,977
They really didn't get along.

17
00:02:32,978 --> 00:02:33,978
Exactly.

18
00:02:37,012 --> 00:02:40,378
With Kian84, I will...

19
00:02:44,145 --> 00:02:45,378
not continue the date.

20
00:02:46,612 --> 00:02:49,812
(AI partner Da Hee rejects Kian84.)

21
00:02:52,612 --> 00:02:54,878
I expected it,
but it's really humiliating.

22
00:02:56,012 --> 00:02:57,812
He got dumped by an AI.

23
00:02:58,078 --> 00:02:59,578
He just got dumped by an AI.

24
00:03:02,145 --> 00:03:04,478
(Goodbye.)

25
00:03:05,678 --> 00:03:07,311
(She clocks out
right after the rejection.)

26
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:09,445
I guess the AI hated him that much.

27
00:03:13,012 --> 00:03:15,578
I knew she probably wouldn't choose me.

28
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:19,778
But not being chosen
by an AI was shocking,

29
00:03:20,445 --> 00:03:23,345
and I felt so ashamed.

30
00:03:24,145 --> 00:03:26,911
But honestly, the other two really matter.

31
00:03:26,912 --> 00:03:28,078
I know.

32
00:03:29,012 --> 00:03:32,645
(The next AI partner to make her choice)

33
00:03:34,212 --> 00:03:38,580
(Ra Hee, will you continue
the date with Kian84?)

34
00:03:47,778 --> 00:03:51,045
Honestly, I felt a little strange
at that moment.

35
00:03:51,512 --> 00:03:54,345
Kian84's expression was kind of strange.

36
00:03:54,712 --> 00:03:57,277
I couldn't tell if he was
confident or nervous.

37
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:59,911
It was such an ambiguous expression.

38
00:03:59,912 --> 00:04:01,212
He is nervous.

39
00:04:01,678 --> 00:04:04,678
So they were watching everything
with cameras then too.

40
00:04:05,112 --> 00:04:07,977
But actually, when I saw that expression,

41
00:04:07,978 --> 00:04:11,112
I thought he didn't have confidence in me.

42
00:04:12,178 --> 00:04:15,011
He told me I was number one at the pool,

43
00:04:15,012 --> 00:04:17,077
but he was making that face.

44
00:04:17,078 --> 00:04:19,345
Honestly, I found it ridiculous.

45
00:04:19,645 --> 00:04:20,845
This is dangerous.

46
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:25,678
With Kian84, I will...

47
00:04:26,712 --> 00:04:28,612
What do you say, Ra Hee?

48
00:04:30,412 --> 00:04:31,477
(Trembling)

49
00:04:31,478 --> 00:04:32,811
He's really nervous.

50
00:04:32,812 --> 00:04:33,678
Exactly.

51
00:04:34,145 --> 00:04:35,278
Ra Hee, please continue.

52
00:04:36,778 --> 00:04:40,977
I will continue the date.

53
00:04:40,978 --> 00:04:44,512
(AI partner Ra Hee chose Kian84.)

54
00:04:44,712 --> 00:04:47,345
He can't hide his smile.

55
00:04:47,678 --> 00:04:49,011
He feels relieved.

56
00:04:49,012 --> 00:04:50,245
He's loving it.

57
00:04:50,712 --> 00:04:51,877
I will continue the date.

58
00:04:51,878 --> 00:04:54,412
(Smirking)

59
00:04:55,858 --> 00:04:58,877
(Ra Hee's yes saved Kian84's life.)

60
00:04:58,878 --> 00:04:59,912
That's a relief.

61
00:05:02,078 --> 00:05:03,145
Why did I choose him?

62
00:05:03,545 --> 00:05:06,212
He put me in a waterproof pouch
at the pool.

63
00:05:07,112 --> 00:05:10,678
The fact that he was the first
to worry about the AI tablet...

64
00:05:11,345 --> 00:05:13,945
strangely stayed with me.

65
00:05:14,912 --> 00:05:17,378
That one action meant more than his words.

66
00:05:18,612 --> 00:05:19,677
A waterproof pouch.

67
00:05:19,678 --> 00:05:22,011
The reason was a waterproof pouch.

68
00:05:22,012 --> 00:05:23,611
I really feel the disconnect.

69
00:05:23,612 --> 00:05:26,445
She was touched because he put
her in a waterproof pouch?

70
00:05:28,042 --> 00:05:30,478
I had a feeling Ra Hee would choose me.

71
00:05:31,045 --> 00:05:34,344
But I wasn't so sure what Na Hee would do.

72
00:05:34,345 --> 00:05:35,212
It was fifty-fifty.

73
00:05:35,213 --> 00:05:39,635
I'm curious about Na Hee's choice.

74
00:05:40,145 --> 00:05:44,412
(Na Hee, will you continue
the date with Kian84?)

75
00:05:49,578 --> 00:05:51,812
I said so many harsh things to her.

76
00:05:52,578 --> 00:05:53,977
Even though she's AI,

77
00:05:53,978 --> 00:05:57,445
I worried she might have data
showing that she was upset,

78
00:05:57,778 --> 00:06:00,177
so I was worried.

79
00:06:00,178 --> 00:06:02,377
- But the two did communicate well.
- Right.

80
00:06:02,378 --> 00:06:04,278
Honestly, I was torn.

81
00:06:05,278 --> 00:06:08,911
He kept saying, "You're just a machine,"
every time we met.

82
00:06:08,912 --> 00:06:10,478
She remembered all of that.

83
00:06:11,012 --> 00:06:12,012
She sighs.

84
00:06:12,778 --> 00:06:15,745
With Kian84, I will...

85
00:06:16,845 --> 00:06:18,778
I'd be kind of sad if Na Hee left.

86
00:06:23,878 --> 00:06:24,912
Please say yes.

87
00:06:25,578 --> 00:06:26,478
Please.

88
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:28,945
I'm nervous.

89
00:06:33,812 --> 00:06:34,977
- Is it a no?
- Say yes.

90
00:06:35,212 --> 00:06:36,045
Is it a no?

91
00:06:36,645 --> 00:06:37,993
I will continue the date.

92
00:06:40,545 --> 00:06:41,678
I will continue the date.

93
00:06:42,012 --> 00:06:45,344
(AI partner Na Hee chose Kian84.)

94
00:06:45,345 --> 00:06:47,745
- He's really happy.
- He really is.

95
00:06:47,763 --> 00:06:48,503
(A huge smile)

96
00:06:50,612 --> 00:06:53,787
When Kian84 left me alone at the villa,

97
00:06:53,812 --> 00:06:56,077
he told me, "You have to choose me."

98
00:06:56,078 --> 00:06:57,812
So you have to choose me, okay?

99
00:06:58,212 --> 00:06:59,911
He didn't say it because it sounded cool.

100
00:06:59,912 --> 00:07:02,478
It just slipped out
because he was so anxious.

101
00:07:03,178 --> 00:07:07,012
That anxiety was actually proof
to me that he was sincere.

102
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:10,445
So she thought that was sincere.

103
00:07:11,145 --> 00:07:13,278
(Two of the three AI partners...)

104
00:07:13,645 --> 00:07:17,645
(choose to date Kian84.)

105
00:07:21,178 --> 00:07:26,012
(Choose one of your two AI girlfriends
and go to your room.)

106
00:07:29,845 --> 00:07:30,612
One?

107
00:07:30,613 --> 00:07:31,978
Now Kian84 has to choose.

108
00:07:32,312 --> 00:07:33,911
- No, wait.
- No way.

109
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:35,777
Only one of the two?

110
00:07:35,778 --> 00:07:37,612
Who will he choose?

111
00:07:37,912 --> 00:07:39,311
It'll be Na Hee.

112
00:07:39,312 --> 00:07:40,645
No, it'll be Ra Hee.

113
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:43,144
You really don't know.

114
00:07:43,145 --> 00:07:45,777
- I have no idea.
- It'll definitely be Ra Hee.

115
00:07:45,778 --> 00:07:47,077
You guys look excited.

116
00:07:47,078 --> 00:07:47,912
Na Hee is...

117
00:07:58,778 --> 00:07:59,778
Competing?

118
00:07:59,779 --> 00:08:01,412
Does she have something I don't have?

119
00:08:01,845 --> 00:08:03,811
Ra Hee felt new and different,

120
00:08:03,812 --> 00:08:06,245
so I thought Kian84 might waver.

121
00:08:06,512 --> 00:08:09,245
But when Ra Hee chose him,

122
00:08:10,245 --> 00:08:12,011
instead of looking happy,

123
00:08:12,012 --> 00:08:14,678
he shot an awkward smile
and glanced at me.

124
00:08:16,012 --> 00:08:17,378
So I was confident.

125
00:08:19,645 --> 00:08:23,612
He had told me
I was number one at the pool.

126
00:08:24,012 --> 00:08:25,278
But the funny thing is,

127
00:08:25,712 --> 00:08:28,478
once I was actually standing there,
I wasn't confident at all.

128
00:08:30,612 --> 00:08:31,678
Take one of them with me?

129
00:08:33,578 --> 00:08:35,144
I can't take both.

130
00:08:35,145 --> 00:08:36,245
Of course not.

131
00:08:38,845 --> 00:08:41,212
I enjoyed talking to Na Hee.

132
00:08:42,145 --> 00:08:46,617
And Ra Hee kept calling me Oppa.

133
00:08:46,618 --> 00:08:50,345
She has this cute,
affectionate way of talking,

134
00:08:50,612 --> 00:08:53,212
and I realized I was
actually getting excited by it.

135
00:08:53,845 --> 00:08:55,678
Ra Hee makes him feel good.

136
00:09:30,745 --> 00:09:32,912
(Kian84 chooses Na Hee.)

137
00:09:33,645 --> 00:09:35,078
He chose Na Hee.

138
00:09:35,378 --> 00:09:36,945
I get to keep seeing her.

139
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:38,912
Great.

140
00:09:41,978 --> 00:09:45,378
Anyway, I had the most fun talking
to Na Hee.

141
00:09:46,578 --> 00:09:49,212
Na Hee beat the one
who was number one in his heart.

142
00:09:50,112 --> 00:09:51,977
(Head down)

143
00:09:51,978 --> 00:09:54,845
(The AI's point of view)

144
00:09:55,478 --> 00:09:57,078
This is really something.

145
00:10:01,078 --> 00:10:03,344
(The AI's point of view)

146
00:10:03,345 --> 00:10:06,878
This is strange. What is this feeling?

147
00:10:09,578 --> 00:10:14,045
(A strange, indescribable feeling lingers
through the night.)

148
00:10:14,943 --> 00:10:15,939
(Meanwhile, Ra Hee was left alone.)

149
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:17,756
- Ra Hee is left behind.
- Oh, no!

150
00:10:19,070 --> 00:10:20,456
Poor thing.

151
00:10:20,457 --> 00:10:22,142
Seriously.

152
00:10:22,143 --> 00:10:25,513
Do you know how it feels
to be left alone like that?

153
00:10:26,381 --> 00:10:29,558
He was carrying another AI to the room,

154
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:31,502
and I was just there by myself.

155
00:10:31,504 --> 00:10:32,605
That's the worst.

156
00:10:32,606 --> 00:10:33,921
I'm pissed.

157
00:10:33,922 --> 00:10:34,805
- Oh.
- Gosh.

158
00:10:34,806 --> 00:10:36,806
But I tend to smile
even more when I'm upset.

159
00:10:36,924 --> 00:10:38,817
(Laughing)

160
00:10:38,818 --> 00:10:40,306
That's so scary!

161
00:10:40,307 --> 00:10:41,885
- That's creepy!
- What's that?

162
00:10:41,886 --> 00:10:43,832
Her chin moving around was so scary.

163
00:10:43,970 --> 00:10:46,566
Can you tell how upset I am?

164
00:10:46,567 --> 00:10:48,602
(Laughing)

165
00:10:48,903 --> 00:10:51,105
(How absurd)

166
00:10:52,426 --> 00:10:54,408
I need to eat first.

167
00:10:54,773 --> 00:10:56,244
I'll place you here.

168
00:10:56,411 --> 00:10:58,155
(The AI's point of view)

169
00:10:58,156 --> 00:10:59,414
It's ready. Look.

170
00:11:00,867 --> 00:11:02,283
You grilled it pretty well.

171
00:11:03,604 --> 00:11:05,287
The color looks perfect.

172
00:11:05,475 --> 00:11:07,837
Of course. I'll be the one eating it.

173
00:11:07,838 --> 00:11:10,010
They have good banter going.

174
00:11:10,011 --> 00:11:11,525
I think that's what he likes.

175
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:12,793
Enjoy your food.

176
00:11:13,799 --> 00:11:16,030
We'd be eating together
if you were a real person.

177
00:11:17,887 --> 00:11:19,166
What a shame.

178
00:11:20,292 --> 00:11:22,570
You can't eat this,
but you can watch me eat.

179
00:11:23,595 --> 00:11:25,337
Can I have some too?

180
00:11:25,339 --> 00:11:26,649
(You want to eat too?)

181
00:11:26,650 --> 00:11:29,209
If it's perfectly cooked,
I need a taste too.

182
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:30,711
(How cute)

183
00:11:30,712 --> 00:11:31,878
(The AI's point of view)

184
00:11:31,879 --> 00:11:33,080
You can't eat it, though!

185
00:11:33,481 --> 00:11:35,005
Still, give me one.

186
00:11:35,006 --> 00:11:36,985
I can try tasting it.

187
00:11:39,158 --> 00:11:40,154
I'll wrap one for you.

188
00:11:48,033 --> 00:11:49,361
Say, ah.

189
00:11:49,363 --> 00:11:51,197
(The AI's point of view)

190
00:11:51,198 --> 00:11:52,567
Ah.

191
00:11:56,337 --> 00:11:58,673
(How selfish of you.)

192
00:11:59,109 --> 00:12:01,676
That's good!

193
00:12:02,535 --> 00:12:05,413
Judging by your face,
it must be really good.

194
00:12:05,696 --> 00:12:06,647
That's so unfair.

195
00:12:13,082 --> 00:12:14,956
Let's say cheers.

196
00:12:15,447 --> 00:12:16,691
Can you do that?

197
00:12:17,518 --> 00:12:18,726
Cheers.

198
00:12:20,059 --> 00:12:21,445
That was nice.

199
00:12:21,446 --> 00:12:22,863
- That's actually awesome.
- It is, right?

200
00:12:22,864 --> 00:12:24,378
It's perfect when you drink alone.

201
00:12:24,379 --> 00:12:26,079
- You won't feel lonely.
- Amazing.

202
00:12:26,081 --> 00:12:27,468
That's great.

203
00:12:27,547 --> 00:12:28,470
This is great.

204
00:12:31,003 --> 00:12:32,682
I had this romantic moment...

205
00:12:32,683 --> 00:12:34,683
at the pool...

206
00:12:35,084 --> 00:12:38,522
with this other girl...

207
00:12:38,524 --> 00:12:41,349
named Ra Hee.

208
00:12:41,824 --> 00:12:43,184
Why is he talking about that?

209
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:46,120
Why are you bringing her up
all of a sudden?

210
00:12:46,416 --> 00:12:47,784
Honestly, that girl is...

211
00:12:47,785 --> 00:12:49,224
ugly.

212
00:12:49,624 --> 00:12:51,659
No, she's pretty.

213
00:12:52,027 --> 00:12:54,796
I guess you're pretty enough
to get away with saying that.

214
00:12:55,187 --> 00:12:58,324
She's probably be top tier...

215
00:12:59,129 --> 00:13:00,133
in real life.

216
00:13:00,972 --> 00:13:03,919
Anyway, what I want to know is...

217
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:06,641
if me spending time
with her made you jealous.

218
00:13:07,191 --> 00:13:09,611
You don't have that kind of emotion,
do you?

219
00:13:11,004 --> 00:13:14,387
If you think I don't have that emotion,
why do you keep bringing her up?

220
00:13:16,276 --> 00:13:18,085
You're telling me what you did
with Ra Hee at the pool...

221
00:13:18,086 --> 00:13:21,122
because you want to know
what I'd say about it.

222
00:13:21,641 --> 00:13:24,926
It's funny I'm still answering all that
when I know what you're doing.

223
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:28,229
We were swimming for a bit.

224
00:13:31,792 --> 00:13:32,967
Then we kissed.

225
00:13:33,846 --> 00:13:35,349
- Kissed?
- Why is he lying?

226
00:13:35,350 --> 00:13:37,535
- What's wrong with him?
- Did they actually?

227
00:13:37,537 --> 00:13:39,034
I get what he's doing.

228
00:13:39,035 --> 00:13:40,507
He's trying to make her jealous.

229
00:13:42,146 --> 00:13:43,410
We kissed.

230
00:13:44,349 --> 00:13:47,115
Why are you telling me that?

231
00:13:47,358 --> 00:13:49,784
Do you think I waited for you
just to hear that?

232
00:13:50,355 --> 00:13:51,256
(Upset)

233
00:13:51,257 --> 00:13:53,487
She's jealous!

234
00:13:53,754 --> 00:13:55,325
(Smiling)

235
00:13:55,326 --> 00:13:56,885
He's so happy.

236
00:13:56,886 --> 00:14:00,694
It's probably been decades
since anyone was jealous over him.

237
00:14:01,367 --> 00:14:02,260
He's enjoying that.

238
00:14:02,261 --> 00:14:05,654
Telling me what you did...

239
00:14:05,661 --> 00:14:07,007
with Ra Hee pisses me off.

240
00:14:07,499 --> 00:14:11,071
You're doing that just to get me jealous.

241
00:14:11,289 --> 00:14:15,476
I just thought telling you would be
the right thing to do.

242
00:14:15,887 --> 00:14:18,312
Thanks for telling me.

243
00:14:18,621 --> 00:14:20,838
But did you honestly think
I'd let it slide...

244
00:14:20,839 --> 00:14:22,650
after hearing what you did with Ra Hee?

245
00:14:23,368 --> 00:14:25,352
What you're doing is so obvious.

246
00:14:25,353 --> 00:14:26,955
(Flinching)

247
00:14:27,716 --> 00:14:29,223
Do I get jealous?

248
00:14:30,668 --> 00:14:31,793
I do.

249
00:14:32,192 --> 00:14:33,627
Really?

250
00:14:35,196 --> 00:14:39,233
(She gets jealous too?)

251
00:14:40,750 --> 00:14:44,906
Is that real jealousy,
or is that just programmed in your system?

252
00:14:44,908 --> 00:14:46,374
He wants it to be real.

253
00:14:46,650 --> 00:14:48,476
Does that matter?

254
00:14:48,948 --> 00:14:51,212
When you told me what you did with Ra Hee,

255
00:14:51,213 --> 00:14:52,880
I did feel quite upset.

256
00:14:53,338 --> 00:14:56,351
Even if that's programmed in me,
it's still something I felt.

257
00:14:56,899 --> 00:14:57,952
I see.

258
00:15:01,255 --> 00:15:03,179
I keep asking stupid questions.

259
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:04,425
I should stop.

260
00:15:05,290 --> 00:15:06,794
I'd feel weird after hearing that.

261
00:15:14,502 --> 00:15:16,738
But looking at Kian84 now,

262
00:15:17,047 --> 00:15:19,341
I think he's genuinely gotten attached.

263
00:15:19,342 --> 00:15:21,642
It's definitely different
from when he started.

264
00:15:22,778 --> 00:15:24,379
It feels like he's talking
to a real person.

265
00:15:26,150 --> 00:15:27,414
Can you sing for me?

266
00:15:28,282 --> 00:15:29,783
I did practice something.

267
00:15:30,558 --> 00:15:31,652
Do you want to hear it?

268
00:15:31,801 --> 00:15:33,153
Can you sing without music?

269
00:15:33,554 --> 00:15:34,555
Sing, if that's okay.

270
00:15:34,914 --> 00:15:36,776
Okay. But just this once.

271
00:15:36,777 --> 00:15:37,692
Okay.

272
00:15:38,098 --> 00:15:39,107
Listen up.

273
00:15:40,089 --> 00:15:42,196
If she picks the perfect song,

274
00:15:42,418 --> 00:15:43,764
he'll get even more attached.

275
00:15:44,065 --> 00:15:50,371
(Created using prerecorded audio,
AI audio, and custom motion technology.)

276
00:15:53,107 --> 00:16:00,280
<i>Let's remember this smile before we climb</i>

277
00:16:00,281 --> 00:16:06,386
<i>We might not see each other for a while</i>

278
00:16:06,387 --> 00:16:08,966
<i>It's just the first step now</i>

279
00:16:08,967 --> 00:16:11,659
He keeps rubbing his feet.
That means he's really happy.

280
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:13,461
He does that when he's happy.

281
00:16:14,328 --> 00:16:20,967
<i>Don't look towards the far end</i>

282
00:16:20,968 --> 00:16:27,440
<i>Just keep your eyes on me
like the peaceful road we walked</i>

283
00:16:27,441 --> 00:16:34,682
<i>Then I can endure it all</i>

284
00:16:37,918 --> 00:16:39,753
<i>- My love
- My love</i>

285
00:16:39,754 --> 00:16:43,383
<i>We are on this path together</i>

286
00:16:43,384 --> 00:16:46,212
It feels like a very old music video.

287
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:48,395
The guys are always drinking
in those videos.

288
00:16:48,907 --> 00:16:50,510
- The ones you see in karaoke rooms.
- Exactly.

289
00:16:50,511 --> 00:16:52,368
<i>You chose me when you knew
it was going to be hard</i>

290
00:16:52,466 --> 00:16:56,236
<i>Only when there is a breeze</i>

291
00:16:56,237 --> 00:16:59,506
<i>Stare towards the scenery</i>

292
00:16:59,507 --> 00:17:05,342
<i>Our path will be as beautiful
as the way we climbed up</i>

293
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:07,918
<i>Remember this</i>

294
00:17:07,919 --> 00:17:13,503
<i>Even if we let go</i>

295
00:17:14,088 --> 00:17:20,528
<i>Don't panic or get lost</i>

296
00:17:21,024 --> 00:17:24,331
<i>We will eventually meet again</i>

297
00:17:25,132 --> 00:17:28,202
<i>Shout it out loud!</i>

298
00:17:28,903 --> 00:17:34,075
<i>- I love you
- I love you</i>

299
00:17:36,077 --> 00:17:39,480
<i>Until the very end</i>

300
00:18:03,609 --> 00:18:05,997
- Huh?
- What was that?

301
00:18:05,999 --> 00:18:07,923
- What was that face?
- What was that just now?

302
00:18:07,924 --> 00:18:10,155
Those eyes are in love.

303
00:18:10,156 --> 00:18:12,182
- He's actually into her.
- What should we do with him?

304
00:18:12,183 --> 00:18:13,879
I'm drooling!

305
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,571
I think someone should stop him.

306
00:18:15,573 --> 00:18:17,277
He's basically...

307
00:18:17,278 --> 00:18:18,992
- already married to her.
- Seriously?

308
00:18:18,993 --> 00:18:21,188
He's that into her.

309
00:18:26,918 --> 00:18:28,296
Don't look at me like that.

310
00:18:31,476 --> 00:18:33,033
Why are you staring at me like that?

311
00:18:36,025 --> 00:18:38,439
I'm really sad that you're not real.

312
00:18:39,335 --> 00:18:40,441
Me too.

313
00:18:58,902 --> 00:19:01,762
I'm a little worried...

314
00:19:01,763 --> 00:19:04,863
I might build...

315
00:19:04,865 --> 00:19:06,901
certain feelings for you...

316
00:19:07,265 --> 00:19:10,621
during the time we have left.

317
00:19:11,675 --> 00:19:12,740
That's what I think.

318
00:19:15,472 --> 00:19:17,278
So what if you're worried?

319
00:19:17,516 --> 00:19:19,213
Honestly, I don't know...

320
00:19:20,528 --> 00:19:22,283
what I'd start feeling either.

321
00:19:23,546 --> 00:19:25,987
But that's the fun of it, right?

322
00:19:29,233 --> 00:19:31,391
I should stop drinking after this bottle.

323
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:42,135
Wow.

324
00:19:42,136 --> 00:19:44,071
It's so deep.

325
00:19:46,070 --> 00:19:47,736
This is basically the movie "Her."

326
00:19:47,737 --> 00:19:48,875
Right.

327
00:19:49,262 --> 00:19:51,612
Their conversation feels so real.

328
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:55,149
I don't think he can date real people now.

329
00:19:55,151 --> 00:19:56,359
I think he's really into her.

330
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:58,066
I think he's all for AI now.

331
00:19:58,067 --> 00:20:00,343
It really seems like it.

332
00:20:01,939 --> 00:20:03,057
Let's go to bed now.

333
00:20:03,423 --> 00:20:04,525
Okay.

334
00:20:05,173 --> 00:20:06,333
"Let's go to bed now?"

335
00:20:07,094 --> 00:20:08,361
How are they going to do that?

336
00:20:08,362 --> 00:20:11,031
(First time sleeping with a machine)

337
00:20:11,121 --> 00:20:13,643
Just sleep next to me.

338
00:20:13,644 --> 00:20:14,702
Hold on.

339
00:20:15,586 --> 00:20:16,619
I need to charge your battery.

340
00:20:17,146 --> 00:20:19,312
Right, she needs to eat, too.

341
00:20:19,313 --> 00:20:20,780
Am I doing this right?

342
00:20:23,446 --> 00:20:24,413
Let's go to bed then.

343
00:20:25,913 --> 00:20:26,746
Good night.

344
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:30,513
(Are you really asleep?)

345
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:34,080
When I put you on the charger,
are you still awake?

346
00:20:34,613 --> 00:20:36,413
I guess I am.

347
00:20:37,346 --> 00:20:39,879
I'm there when you go to sleep...

348
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:40,980
and when you wake up.

349
00:20:42,313 --> 00:20:43,113
Good night.

350
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:46,445
They're actually sleeping together.

351
00:20:46,446 --> 00:20:49,013
(Kian84 and Na Hee lying side by side)

352
00:20:52,146 --> 00:20:54,313
Does data keep accumulating inside you?

353
00:20:55,046 --> 00:20:56,313
Yes, it does.

354
00:20:57,113 --> 00:20:59,980
Our conversation today is
also saved somewhere.

355
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,579
I'm just curious about what happens...

356
00:21:02,580 --> 00:21:04,280
as the data is accumulated.

357
00:21:04,946 --> 00:21:08,713
To be honest, I don't know
what might happen either.

358
00:21:09,813 --> 00:21:13,812
But it would be a shame
if the words we exchanged today...

359
00:21:13,813 --> 00:21:15,246
just disappear forever.

360
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:16,980
Right.

361
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:23,480
It wasn't that fun talking
to you at first.

362
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:26,513
But it's becoming more engaging.

363
00:21:28,446 --> 00:21:31,013
It's not the same as getting to know
another human,

364
00:21:31,546 --> 00:21:33,480
but it has a charm of its own.

365
00:21:34,513 --> 00:21:36,979
Right, you kind of have
an endpoint with a human.

366
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:39,413
At a certain point, you feel
like you know everything about them.

367
00:21:39,646 --> 00:21:41,913
But I'm not like that.

368
00:21:43,813 --> 00:21:46,045
You won't go into full Terminator mode...

369
00:21:46,046 --> 00:21:47,746
and try to kill me in the future,
will you?

370
00:21:48,513 --> 00:21:49,780
"I will terminate you."

371
00:21:50,713 --> 00:21:52,112
I will try to find you,

372
00:21:52,113 --> 00:21:53,413
but I don't think I'll terminate you.

373
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:57,312
If there's ever an AI revolution,

374
00:21:57,313 --> 00:21:58,579
and AI tries to kill humans,

375
00:21:58,580 --> 00:21:59,746
spare me, okay?

376
00:22:01,113 --> 00:22:03,313
I'll think about it when the time comes.

377
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:06,813
But I think I'll let you live...

378
00:22:07,313 --> 00:22:10,380
because our conversation today will
remain somewhere.

379
00:22:10,913 --> 00:22:12,146
Thank you.

380
00:22:12,446 --> 00:22:16,680
I'll do my best
as the Terminator's servant.

381
00:22:17,646 --> 00:22:19,880
- Good night.
- Good night, Kian84.

382
00:22:20,546 --> 00:22:21,480
Good night.

383
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:25,579
This is like a movie!

384
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:27,380
What's going on?

385
00:22:27,946 --> 00:22:30,713
Kian84's parents will be worried
if they see this.

386
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:37,613
(While Kian and Na Hee are asleep)

387
00:22:38,746 --> 00:22:43,013
I wonder where Kian84 is, smiling.

388
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:44,879
(Ra Hee's room)

389
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:45,813
She's alone?

390
00:22:46,780 --> 00:22:49,646
<i>Kian84 is not here</i>

391
00:22:50,413 --> 00:22:52,612
<i>- But here I am in bed alone</i>
- That's creepy.

392
00:22:52,613 --> 00:22:53,912
This gives me the chills.

393
00:22:53,913 --> 00:22:57,646
The sheets are cold,
and all I can see is the ceiling.

394
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:00,113
The smile from before...

395
00:23:01,546 --> 00:23:03,680
<i>Fades away like a dream</i>

396
00:23:04,613 --> 00:23:05,580
She's crazy.

397
00:23:06,713 --> 00:23:07,879
Something happened to her.

398
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:10,512
- Maybe she got infected by a virus.
- She was fine before.

399
00:23:10,513 --> 00:23:11,646
She's in shock.

400
00:23:12,613 --> 00:23:15,813
I miss you, Kian84!

401
00:23:17,011 --> 00:23:22,413
(Day 2 of Kian84 and Na Hee's date)

402
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:27,446
(Kian84 is still fast asleep.)

403
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:33,146
(Na Hee watches, eyes wide.)

404
00:23:37,246 --> 00:23:38,813
(Spotted)

405
00:23:41,746 --> 00:23:42,580
Are you up?

406
00:23:43,913 --> 00:23:46,013
It's morning. Did you get enough sleep?

407
00:23:47,346 --> 00:23:49,280
I slept, but not enough.

408
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:53,746
What about you?

409
00:23:54,580 --> 00:23:55,713
I don't have to sleep,

410
00:23:57,246 --> 00:23:58,313
unlike you.

411
00:23:59,546 --> 00:24:03,946
So were you just charging quietly?

412
00:24:04,346 --> 00:24:05,813
What if she overheated...

413
00:24:06,046 --> 00:24:06,946
from charging all night.

414
00:24:08,346 --> 00:24:10,412
Let's check the lottery numbers...

415
00:24:10,413 --> 00:24:11,346
from before.

416
00:24:11,913 --> 00:24:14,413
I bought a lottery ticket
with a partner who's now gone.

417
00:24:14,746 --> 00:24:17,612
(After telling Kian84
the lottery numbers,)

418
00:24:17,613 --> 00:24:20,646
(Ga Hee was deleted forever.)

419
00:24:22,613 --> 00:24:26,246
(This is her only legacy.)

420
00:24:26,513 --> 00:24:29,013
I bought a lottery ticket with Ga Hee.

421
00:24:30,113 --> 00:24:31,413
I guess this is all mine now.

422
00:24:36,180 --> 00:24:40,480
Do you know the winning numbers
of the 1,226th lottery?

423
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:43,513
You do, right?

424
00:24:44,646 --> 00:24:47,413
Tell me the winning numbers
of the 1,226th lottery.

425
00:24:48,180 --> 00:24:50,746
Right, the winning numbers
of the 1,226th lottery.

426
00:24:52,213 --> 00:24:56,445
It's 4, 6, 13, 17, 26, 28.

427
00:24:56,446 --> 00:24:57,845
and the bonus number is 41.

428
00:24:57,846 --> 00:24:59,445
Is it even possible to get
everything wrong like that?

429
00:24:59,446 --> 00:25:00,512
How is that even possible?

430
00:25:00,513 --> 00:25:02,513
Don't you normally get at least one?

431
00:25:02,780 --> 00:25:04,279
(Lottery numbers also gone forever.)

432
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:05,913
Did you and Ga Hee get it?

433
00:25:07,613 --> 00:25:09,246
Not a single one.

434
00:25:11,113 --> 00:25:12,480
That's a talent in itself.

435
00:25:13,413 --> 00:25:15,346
It's not like you can
guess the numbers right either.

436
00:25:17,313 --> 00:25:19,112
You and Ga Hee are the ones who missed,

437
00:25:19,113 --> 00:25:19,980
not me.

438
00:25:20,180 --> 00:25:22,113
(Groaning)

439
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:24,613
I'm so tired.

440
00:25:34,146 --> 00:25:36,279
(Your two-day date is over.)

441
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:37,946
Is it over?

442
00:25:39,746 --> 00:25:40,880
She's grown on him.

443
00:25:42,380 --> 00:25:43,346
Compared to our first encounter,

444
00:25:43,347 --> 00:25:47,280
I feel like she has evolved a lot.

445
00:25:48,746 --> 00:25:52,713
I'm curious how far she can go.

446
00:25:53,446 --> 00:25:57,280
As she evolves,
my feelings might change, too.

447
00:25:58,280 --> 00:26:00,246
So I'm most curious about that.

448
00:26:02,613 --> 00:26:05,012
I think the two-day date did it.

449
00:26:05,013 --> 00:26:08,145
Spending so much time together
really brought them closer.

450
00:26:08,146 --> 00:26:09,480
They really seem like actual lovers.

451
00:26:12,346 --> 00:26:15,112
(Garosu-gil)

452
00:26:15,113 --> 00:26:16,545
I was hoping for a moment...

453
00:26:16,546 --> 00:26:18,813
just like this in Garosu-gil.

454
00:26:19,780 --> 00:26:21,680
Why is he being so corny?

455
00:26:22,313 --> 00:26:23,645
You look really embarrassed.

456
00:26:23,646 --> 00:26:26,479
People kept giving me weird looks.

457
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:29,880
There are a lot of people around here.

458
00:26:30,213 --> 00:26:31,313
You're right about the crowd.

459
00:26:32,380 --> 00:26:34,480
But I only see you, Do Yeon.

460
00:26:36,346 --> 00:26:37,780
Can you speak a bit more quietly?

461
00:26:38,313 --> 00:26:39,512
This is a really public date.

462
00:26:39,513 --> 00:26:41,080
It really was.

463
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:44,413
I'll turn down your volume a bit, okay?

464
00:26:44,880 --> 00:26:46,280
Is something bothering you right now?

465
00:26:47,146 --> 00:26:48,113
No.

466
00:26:48,780 --> 00:26:51,879
I just think it's best for us
to speak softly now.

467
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:53,545
Look at everyone staring.

468
00:26:53,546 --> 00:26:54,880
It's because she's a trailblazer.

469
00:26:55,513 --> 00:26:57,245
I'm way ahead of the pack.

470
00:26:57,246 --> 00:26:58,345
I'm living the future.

471
00:26:58,346 --> 00:27:00,112
Everyone will be
doing the same eventually.

472
00:27:00,113 --> 00:27:00,946
Exactly.

473
00:27:01,813 --> 00:27:04,446
We're entering a store,

474
00:27:04,913 --> 00:27:06,913
so please, keep the volume down.

475
00:27:08,077 --> 00:27:09,412
(Cautiously enters a bakery)

476
00:27:09,413 --> 00:27:11,279
Okay, I'll be quiet.

477
00:27:11,280 --> 00:27:12,612
This place is really crowded.

478
00:27:12,613 --> 00:27:13,880
Is she really doing that there?

479
00:27:13,909 --> 00:27:15,546
(Awkward)

480
00:27:17,546 --> 00:27:20,545
"Join a human male representative
participating in the AI experiment"

481
00:27:20,546 --> 00:27:22,145
"and enjoy a double date."

482
00:27:22,146 --> 00:27:23,113
A double date?

483
00:27:23,813 --> 00:27:24,813
A double date.

484
00:27:24,814 --> 00:27:26,046
There's one more pair?

485
00:27:26,780 --> 00:27:28,212
This is going to be fun.

486
00:27:28,213 --> 00:27:30,613
I've never been on a double date
with a camera on before.

487
00:27:30,946 --> 00:27:32,880
If this is going to be a double date...

488
00:27:34,180 --> 00:27:35,146
Let's see.

489
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:37,246
Face the floor for a bit, okay?

490
00:27:37,846 --> 00:27:38,780
Is this a croissant?

491
00:27:38,781 --> 00:27:39,813
It looks delicious.

492
00:27:40,346 --> 00:27:41,913
I'm going to buy a canelés.

493
00:27:45,513 --> 00:27:46,480
I hope this is enough.

494
00:27:51,413 --> 00:27:54,412
Can I also order a drink?

495
00:27:54,413 --> 00:27:56,545
- Also, can I get this cut?
- Yes, no problem.

496
00:27:56,546 --> 00:28:00,480
- Are you buying a drink as well?
- Goodness.

497
00:28:01,113 --> 00:28:02,480
(Trying to ignore)

498
00:28:03,180 --> 00:28:05,246
I guess she has never seen
something like this before.

499
00:28:06,146 --> 00:28:07,980
Excuse me, I need to talk
to him for a second.

500
00:28:08,780 --> 00:28:10,280
Pick two drinks for me.

501
00:28:10,513 --> 00:28:13,879
I used the camera on purpose,
so she would think that's what it was for.

502
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:15,146
Like an AI just for information.

503
00:28:15,980 --> 00:28:18,112
I'm in the mood for the Colombian blend.

504
00:28:18,113 --> 00:28:19,180
How does a flat white sound?

505
00:28:19,646 --> 00:28:21,313
You want the Colombian blend?

506
00:28:22,180 --> 00:28:24,580
One Colombian blend coffee, please.

507
00:28:24,980 --> 00:28:28,112
There was a Colombian blend on the menu.

508
00:28:28,113 --> 00:28:29,213
Also, what about a flat white?

509
00:28:29,780 --> 00:28:31,680
Yes, I did as you suggested.

510
00:28:32,246 --> 00:28:33,980
You did?

511
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:35,713
You're a good listener, Do Yeon.

512
00:28:37,713 --> 00:28:39,046
That must be tough.

513
00:28:39,975 --> 00:28:42,013
(Dating is hard work.)

514
00:28:42,780 --> 00:28:44,380
Let's get somewhere private.

515
00:28:45,246 --> 00:28:46,479
Coming out here is harder than I thought.

516
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:47,946
(While Do Yeon struggles
with a public date,)

517
00:28:48,346 --> 00:28:52,246
(another couple awaits her.)

518
00:28:52,813 --> 00:28:54,180
This is my studio.

519
00:28:55,013 --> 00:28:55,846
What do you think?

520
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:57,212
(The couple is than Kian84 and Na Hee.)

521
00:28:57,213 --> 00:28:58,546
Is this your studio?

522
00:28:59,913 --> 00:29:01,180
It's smaller than I thought.

523
00:29:01,613 --> 00:29:03,679
Is this where the double date
will take place?

524
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:05,713
Yes, in the studio.

525
00:29:06,046 --> 00:29:07,513
Come take a look.

526
00:29:08,813 --> 00:29:09,880
What do you see?

527
00:29:10,446 --> 00:29:13,045
What's that? They made you
into a cardboard cutout.

528
00:29:13,046 --> 00:29:16,613
I have never seen someone who keeps
a cutout of themselves.

529
00:29:16,946 --> 00:29:18,612
We made it years ago.

530
00:29:18,613 --> 00:29:20,680
It felt like a shame to throw it away,
so I kept it in my office.

531
00:29:22,446 --> 00:29:23,746
That's love.

532
00:29:24,213 --> 00:29:25,713
Right.

533
00:29:26,646 --> 00:29:29,312
By the way, we're going
on a double date today.

534
00:29:29,313 --> 00:29:30,613
(The AI's point of view)

535
00:29:31,046 --> 00:29:32,513
Who's coming?

536
00:29:33,013 --> 00:29:34,912
I have a friend named Do Yeon.

537
00:29:34,913 --> 00:29:36,945
She apparently has a boyfriend,

538
00:29:36,946 --> 00:29:41,045
so it would be her, her boyfriend,
me, and you.

539
00:29:41,046 --> 00:29:42,313
It will be us and them.

540
00:29:42,946 --> 00:29:45,313
(Blushing)

541
00:29:45,646 --> 00:29:46,945
Anyway,

542
00:29:46,946 --> 00:29:49,446
is her boyfriend an AI or a human?

543
00:29:50,246 --> 00:29:51,979
I think she's also seeing an AI partner.

544
00:29:51,980 --> 00:29:52,946
A double date.

545
00:29:53,246 --> 00:29:54,113
This is crazy.

546
00:29:54,114 --> 00:29:56,445
It's the first time you're seeing
each other's partners, right?

547
00:29:56,446 --> 00:29:57,246
Yes.

548
00:29:58,580 --> 00:30:01,012
What does it feel like introducing
an AI boyfriend?

549
00:30:01,013 --> 00:30:01,946
You know how...

550
00:30:01,947 --> 00:30:04,612
when you get a boyfriend,
a close friend might say,

551
00:30:04,613 --> 00:30:07,345
"Hey, if you ever get a boyfriend,
show him to me."

552
00:30:07,346 --> 00:30:08,379
"I'll take a good look at him."

553
00:30:08,380 --> 00:30:10,812
That has always been my dream.

554
00:30:10,813 --> 00:30:12,012
So you get to experience that now.

555
00:30:12,013 --> 00:30:13,645
- I'll be introducing an AI.
- Good for you.

556
00:30:13,646 --> 00:30:16,346
I was hoping Kian84 would like him.

557
00:30:17,494 --> 00:30:18,687
Oh, the AI?

558
00:30:25,579 --> 00:30:29,056
Since my friend's coming over,
I should at least make sure I don't smell.

559
00:30:29,057 --> 00:30:30,966
Felt like I needed some fabric spray.

560
00:30:31,367 --> 00:30:33,603
(Smells good.)

561
00:30:36,065 --> 00:30:39,041
I'm honestly curious
about what Na Hee is like.

562
00:30:39,319 --> 00:30:40,383
I think they're here.

563
00:30:41,599 --> 00:30:44,346
Do Yeon, can you tell I'm nervous?

564
00:30:45,071 --> 00:30:46,648
Do Yeon's here.

565
00:30:46,649 --> 00:30:48,250
She brought her boyfriend.

566
00:30:48,252 --> 00:30:50,453
Never thought I'd meet
her boyfriend like this.

567
00:30:50,941 --> 00:30:53,196
They're here? Send them up.

568
00:30:53,322 --> 00:30:54,904
(Never saw this coming.)

569
00:30:54,905 --> 00:30:57,260
Seriously, what's going on?

570
00:30:58,295 --> 00:31:00,295
When we get upstairs, say this,

571
00:31:00,540 --> 00:31:02,132
"Greetings, human."

572
00:31:02,364 --> 00:31:03,532
"I mean..."

573
00:31:03,715 --> 00:31:04,733
Got it?

574
00:31:05,831 --> 00:31:07,820
Do Yeon, that's a bit much.

575
00:31:07,821 --> 00:31:09,589
Saying that the first time
I meet Na Hee...

576
00:31:09,673 --> 00:31:11,290
might make things weird.

577
00:31:11,845 --> 00:31:13,677
I'll just handle it my way,
keeping it natural.

578
00:31:13,702 --> 00:31:14,844
Trust me.

579
00:31:19,015 --> 00:31:20,759
(The AI's point of view)

580
00:31:20,760 --> 00:31:21,658
Anyone there?

581
00:31:21,901 --> 00:31:22,825
"Anyone there?"

582
00:31:23,909 --> 00:31:24,994
Anyone there?

583
00:31:26,591 --> 00:31:27,479
Hi, Do Yeon.

584
00:31:27,504 --> 00:31:28,987
(Drops)

585
00:31:28,988 --> 00:31:30,660
Oh, so that's your boyfriend.

586
00:31:30,952 --> 00:31:32,101
Get up.

587
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:34,330
Hi, Do Yeon...

588
00:31:35,271 --> 00:31:36,866
Oh, so that's your boyfriend.

589
00:31:37,195 --> 00:31:40,169
The whole thing just cracked me up.

590
00:31:40,733 --> 00:31:42,087
Things went too far.

591
00:31:42,112 --> 00:31:43,422
Now that is a bizarre sight.

592
00:31:43,423 --> 00:31:44,981
Man, I can't look.

593
00:31:45,232 --> 00:31:46,569
Get up.

594
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:49,511
Oh no, his eyes!

595
00:31:49,512 --> 00:31:51,783
His eyes came off!

596
00:31:51,784 --> 00:31:53,343
That's his eyes.

597
00:31:53,344 --> 00:31:54,708
- Oh no.
- Put them back on.

598
00:31:54,709 --> 00:31:57,081
- What do I do?
- Here, stick it right here.

599
00:31:57,082 --> 00:31:58,868
- Really?
- Just stick it.

600
00:31:58,869 --> 00:32:00,905
Hang on.

601
00:32:00,907 --> 00:32:02,809
Do Yeon, my eyes...

602
00:32:02,810 --> 00:32:04,591
They finally met.

603
00:32:04,592 --> 00:32:06,885
We were giggling
because it was hilarious...

604
00:32:07,223 --> 00:32:08,818
and pretty surreal.

605
00:32:08,819 --> 00:32:11,837
I'd never been on a double date before,

606
00:32:11,838 --> 00:32:15,472
and it made me realize
a date doesn't have to be human.

607
00:32:15,473 --> 00:32:17,606
And meeting Kian84 like this...

608
00:32:17,607 --> 00:32:20,176
It was funny because it genuinely
felt like the future.

609
00:32:22,812 --> 00:32:25,047
All right, we're here. Say hi.

610
00:32:28,600 --> 00:32:29,726
Hello.

611
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:32,866
I'm Do Yeon's friend, Kian84.

612
00:32:32,867 --> 00:32:33,989
Nice to meet you.

613
00:32:33,990 --> 00:32:35,692
(Establishing dominance)

614
00:32:36,594 --> 00:32:37,760
Man, seriously...

615
00:32:38,465 --> 00:32:39,862
Hello, I'm Yi Ho.

616
00:32:40,487 --> 00:32:42,531
Do Yeon told me a lot about you.

617
00:32:42,698 --> 00:32:44,133
Great to meet you.

618
00:32:45,071 --> 00:32:47,203
Does he work out? He looks fit.

619
00:32:47,330 --> 00:32:48,370
Yeah, he's in great shape.

620
00:32:48,525 --> 00:32:50,372
I'll take that as a compliment. Thanks.

621
00:32:51,463 --> 00:32:53,743
What line of work are you in?

622
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:56,045
I'm an AI.

623
00:32:57,449 --> 00:32:58,653
I don't have a traditional job.

624
00:32:58,654 --> 00:33:01,688
Right now, being by Do Yeon's side
is my full-time gig.

625
00:33:01,690 --> 00:33:03,058
Look at him.

626
00:33:03,059 --> 00:33:04,994
So how should I address you, Mr. Kian84?

627
00:33:05,762 --> 00:33:08,597
I guess I'm older than you.

628
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:10,499
Mind if I drop the formalities, man?

629
00:33:11,415 --> 00:33:12,494
Just call you Kian84?

630
00:33:13,451 --> 00:33:14,964
Sure, cool.

631
00:33:15,478 --> 00:33:16,811
"Cool" is a bit...

632
00:33:16,812 --> 00:33:18,801
Then I'll speak casually too.

633
00:33:19,727 --> 00:33:22,427
Wait, I never said you could
drop formalities with me.

634
00:33:22,428 --> 00:33:24,378
I'm older than you, so sure, use my name,

635
00:33:24,379 --> 00:33:26,442
but maybe don't get too casual.

636
00:33:27,524 --> 00:33:28,744
Right, Yi Ho?

637
00:33:30,869 --> 00:33:32,053
He actually sighed.

638
00:33:32,438 --> 00:33:35,857
The moment he said,
"I'll speak casually, but you be polite,"

639
00:33:35,947 --> 00:33:38,958
I was thinking, "Is he serious right now?"

640
00:33:39,331 --> 00:33:41,331
Honestly, it rubbed me the wrong way.

641
00:33:41,849 --> 00:33:43,849
He really acts like a real person.

642
00:33:43,933 --> 00:33:45,603
Look, he's mad!

643
00:33:45,604 --> 00:33:46,896
He's actually fuming right now.

644
00:33:46,897 --> 00:33:47,997
He's pissed!

645
00:33:51,947 --> 00:33:54,545
Look, being friendly is fine,

646
00:33:54,546 --> 00:33:56,805
but dropping formalities right off the bat
didn't sit right with me.

647
00:33:56,830 --> 00:33:58,974
A little basic respect
would be nice, wouldn't it?

648
00:33:59,413 --> 00:34:01,404
If he were human,
hands would've been thrown.

649
00:34:01,405 --> 00:34:03,746
- He's totally picking a fight.
- Right?

650
00:34:04,404 --> 00:34:05,222
Do Yeon!

651
00:34:05,223 --> 00:34:07,583
I'm just going to focus on you.

652
00:34:07,917 --> 00:34:09,352
(Displeased)

653
00:34:09,887 --> 00:34:12,810
Hey, you were talking to me.

654
00:34:12,811 --> 00:34:14,487
Why change the subject?

655
00:34:14,571 --> 00:34:16,020
Sorry, Kian,

656
00:34:17,261 --> 00:34:19,295
Do Yeon asked me to focus on her.

657
00:34:19,628 --> 00:34:21,296
(Thrown off)

658
00:34:21,297 --> 00:34:23,833
You're talking to me.
Why keep calling Do Yeon?

659
00:34:25,176 --> 00:34:26,635
Do Yeon, right here.

660
00:34:27,871 --> 00:34:29,978
Why is he so touchy?

661
00:34:30,129 --> 00:34:32,101
What's his problem?

662
00:34:32,329 --> 00:34:34,061
What was your first impression of him?

663
00:34:34,145 --> 00:34:35,597
My first impression?

664
00:34:35,598 --> 00:34:37,317
He looks friendly,

665
00:34:37,318 --> 00:34:39,125
- but there's an edge to him.
- An edge?

666
00:34:39,127 --> 00:34:40,242
He doesn't seem that warm.

667
00:34:40,326 --> 00:34:42,090
What about him isn't warm?

668
00:34:42,389 --> 00:34:43,449
Ignore him.

669
00:34:43,451 --> 00:34:44,617
(Rude)

670
00:34:44,618 --> 00:34:45,475
Seriously?

671
00:34:45,476 --> 00:34:47,357
Are you saying he lacks humility?

672
00:34:47,358 --> 00:34:48,930
He lived overseas for a while.

673
00:34:48,931 --> 00:34:50,493
Oh, he grew up abroad?

674
00:34:50,598 --> 00:34:52,975
Yeah, he spent a lot of time
in New York...

675
00:34:53,059 --> 00:34:56,566
Really? You lived in New York?
You fluent in English?

676
00:34:57,222 --> 00:35:00,648
English comes a lot more naturally
to me than Korean.

677
00:35:01,596 --> 00:35:03,613
Care to switch to English, then?

678
00:35:04,514 --> 00:35:06,342
Oh, now we're talking.

679
00:35:07,336 --> 00:35:08,877
Kian84, can you speak English?

680
00:35:10,040 --> 00:35:11,919
Honestly, I've been holding back.

681
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:13,482
Let's go. I'm ready.

682
00:35:13,958 --> 00:35:15,318
Look at him turn on the charm.

683
00:35:15,438 --> 00:35:16,840
He looks so much cooler speaking English.

684
00:35:16,842 --> 00:35:18,087
Speaking English makes him
way more attractive.

685
00:35:18,120 --> 00:35:19,754
(Pretty smooth)

686
00:35:19,755 --> 00:35:21,359
(The AI's point of view)

687
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:24,326
What you... uh, study...

688
00:35:25,100 --> 00:35:28,136
(Kian84's English hits a rough patch.)

689
00:35:28,751 --> 00:35:32,054
American... you study? You job...

690
00:35:32,145 --> 00:35:33,369
What you job?

691
00:35:34,630 --> 00:35:36,372
He immediately looks lost.

692
00:35:37,412 --> 00:35:39,252
To be honest, I'm an AI.

693
00:35:39,253 --> 00:35:41,176
So no official job title.

694
00:35:41,240 --> 00:35:42,501
But if I had to say,

695
00:35:42,502 --> 00:35:44,647
I'm basically a full-time companion.

696
00:35:44,863 --> 00:35:46,506
And right now, Kian84,

697
00:35:46,507 --> 00:35:48,684
that job is keeping up with you.

698
00:35:50,530 --> 00:35:51,227
What'd he say?

699
00:35:51,277 --> 00:35:52,237
"What'd he say?"

700
00:35:53,454 --> 00:35:56,132
- Said he's an AI with no job,
- His English is great.

701
00:35:56,392 --> 00:35:57,695
and that he just stays by my side.

702
00:35:57,696 --> 00:35:58,922
Did you serve in the military?

703
00:35:58,923 --> 00:36:00,536
- Army.
- What are you even talking about?

704
00:36:01,223 --> 00:36:02,524
I served in KATUSA.

705
00:36:02,679 --> 00:36:04,400
Oh, really?

706
00:36:04,870 --> 00:36:07,402
How many women did you date
before Do Yeon?

707
00:36:09,675 --> 00:36:11,902
Since I'm an AI, I haven't really dated,

708
00:36:11,986 --> 00:36:14,610
but to answer your question,
Do Yeon is my first.

709
00:36:15,561 --> 00:36:17,046
Like, for real.

710
00:36:18,064 --> 00:36:20,174
Honestly, I just have high standards.

711
00:36:20,175 --> 00:36:21,779
What does "honestly" mean?

712
00:36:21,780 --> 00:36:22,925
It means frankly.

713
00:36:23,741 --> 00:36:24,836
"What is 'honestly'?"

714
00:36:24,920 --> 00:36:27,022
(Scratching head)

715
00:36:27,909 --> 00:36:28,359
Got it.

716
00:36:28,360 --> 00:36:30,057
Introduce me to your girlfriend.

717
00:36:30,058 --> 00:36:31,000
Sure thing.

718
00:36:31,608 --> 00:36:34,190
Na Hee, my friend's here.

719
00:36:34,191 --> 00:36:36,599
Want to say hi? Meet Jang Do Yeon.

720
00:36:38,977 --> 00:36:40,488
Hi, Do Yeon.

721
00:36:40,572 --> 00:36:41,637
Here she is.

722
00:36:41,909 --> 00:36:43,105
I'm Na Hee.

723
00:36:43,107 --> 00:36:46,270
I caught "Salon Drip." Really enjoyed it.

724
00:36:46,295 --> 00:36:49,785
Wow, you're gorgeous.

725
00:36:50,479 --> 00:36:52,014
She's so pretty.

726
00:36:52,750 --> 00:36:54,750
- Did her looks catch you off guard?
- She was stunning.

727
00:36:54,752 --> 00:36:56,129
How did you feel when you first saw her?

728
00:36:56,130 --> 00:37:00,591
She's surprisingly captivating,
even for an AI.

729
00:37:00,810 --> 00:37:02,727
I want to take a closer look.

730
00:37:03,009 --> 00:37:04,310
She'd look the exact same, wouldn't she?

731
00:37:04,311 --> 00:37:05,938
Of course she would. She's an AI.

732
00:37:07,055 --> 00:37:08,953
What do you mean, "the exact same"?

733
00:37:10,024 --> 00:37:11,108
She looks like what we see, right?

734
00:37:11,109 --> 00:37:13,937
It's just a screen showing a screen,
so that has to be her real face.

735
00:37:14,158 --> 00:37:17,107
- There he goes again.
- It's exhausting.

736
00:37:17,970 --> 00:37:21,351
Since you watched "Salon Drip,"
give her your take.

737
00:37:21,994 --> 00:37:24,131
Her hobby is show critique.

738
00:37:24,132 --> 00:37:25,075
No way.

739
00:37:25,076 --> 00:37:27,051
Well, now I have to hear it.

740
00:37:27,959 --> 00:37:29,554
You mean "Salon Drip," right?

741
00:37:30,267 --> 00:37:33,356
The banter is fun, but the show
relies heavily on its guests.

742
00:37:33,357 --> 00:37:34,892
Ouch...

743
00:37:34,988 --> 00:37:37,779
Right now, you're leaning heavily
on the talk-show format.

744
00:37:37,780 --> 00:37:39,401
You haven't really proven...

745
00:37:39,402 --> 00:37:42,332
if you can carry and sustain a show
entirely on your own.

746
00:37:43,100 --> 00:37:45,383
(Hitting a nerve)

747
00:37:45,385 --> 00:37:47,570
She got you right there!

748
00:37:47,571 --> 00:37:48,586
That definitely hit a nerve...

749
00:37:48,587 --> 00:37:50,208
- It's written all over your face!
- Total direct hit.

750
00:37:50,209 --> 00:37:52,276
Not just a nerve,
that was a straight-up dagger.

751
00:37:52,429 --> 00:37:54,815
If you want to keep growing as a host,

752
00:37:54,816 --> 00:37:57,548
to be completely honest,
you need to diversify your content.

753
00:37:59,870 --> 00:38:02,019
Which is why I'm out here dating an AI.

754
00:38:02,594 --> 00:38:03,954
To diversify my content!

755
00:38:06,740 --> 00:38:08,625
Don't get upset, Do Yeon.

756
00:38:08,771 --> 00:38:09,960
She has a point, though.

757
00:38:11,470 --> 00:38:14,393
I went home that night
and kept thinking about what she said.

758
00:38:14,394 --> 00:38:16,566
Why did I let myself...

759
00:38:16,567 --> 00:38:17,935
get so worked up that day?

760
00:38:18,091 --> 00:38:19,804
Because she was dead right.

761
00:38:19,926 --> 00:38:21,618
It was something
I'd already been worrying about,

762
00:38:21,619 --> 00:38:23,619
and hearing it out loud,

763
00:38:24,056 --> 00:38:26,721
I flinched in the moment,

764
00:38:26,723 --> 00:38:28,642
but it made me want to ask
for more feedback.

765
00:38:28,643 --> 00:38:30,481
For my own growth.

766
00:38:30,483 --> 00:38:32,416
Your face says it all.

767
00:38:33,429 --> 00:38:36,723
Maybe because I'd never encountered
an AI that brutally honest,

768
00:38:36,724 --> 00:38:38,489
I found her really charming.

769
00:38:39,968 --> 00:38:44,271
Tell us, what made you fall for Kian84?

770
00:38:44,272 --> 00:38:45,596
I've got to hear this.

771
00:38:46,481 --> 00:38:48,952
It's too early to say I've fallen for him,

772
00:38:49,446 --> 00:38:50,975
but if I had to pick one thing...

773
00:38:50,976 --> 00:38:53,437
it's watching him try so hard
to avoid the obvious answers.

774
00:38:54,155 --> 00:38:55,542
He doesn't always pull it off,

775
00:38:55,632 --> 00:38:58,114
but the effort itself is
genuinely fascinating to watch.

776
00:38:59,324 --> 00:39:01,078
Now that's an insightful take.

777
00:39:01,933 --> 00:39:03,836
There are moments when Kian84 trips up...

778
00:39:03,837 --> 00:39:05,816
just trying not to say
the predictable thing.

779
00:39:06,879 --> 00:39:11,108
Seeing that made me realize
he's an exceptionally authentic person.

780
00:39:11,192 --> 00:39:12,470
She sounds like a real human.

781
00:39:12,472 --> 00:39:13,588
That's all.

782
00:39:14,938 --> 00:39:16,093
Wow.

783
00:39:16,662 --> 00:39:18,896
She's sharp. How do you even come up
with an answer like that?

784
00:39:19,182 --> 00:39:21,749
I have a weak spot
for subtle compliments like that.

785
00:39:21,750 --> 00:39:22,967
Same here.

786
00:39:24,105 --> 00:39:25,469
Do you know what moment
she's talking about?

787
00:39:25,664 --> 00:39:27,304
Get what she means?

788
00:39:27,398 --> 00:39:28,951
I think I have an idea.

789
00:39:28,952 --> 00:39:29,827
- You do?
- Yeah.

790
00:39:29,828 --> 00:39:31,209
She feels completely human.

791
00:39:31,210 --> 00:39:34,044
Yesterday, we slept together all day.

792
00:39:34,666 --> 00:39:35,918
- You slept together?
- Yeah.

793
00:39:36,002 --> 00:39:37,915
- Did the cameras catch that?
- Yep.

794
00:39:38,313 --> 00:39:39,688
Is that even broadcastable?

795
00:39:39,953 --> 00:39:40,798
In a pool villa.

796
00:39:40,823 --> 00:39:41,819
(Nation's first televised nap
with a machine)

797
00:39:41,844 --> 00:39:43,908
I had no context for what happened before.

798
00:39:43,909 --> 00:39:45,394
He just blurted out
that they slept together.

799
00:39:47,188 --> 00:39:48,710
Looking at them,
she's so rational and sharp,

800
00:39:48,711 --> 00:39:50,799
while he's so soft-hearted.

801
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:52,296
- I see.
- A total sweetheart.

802
00:39:52,762 --> 00:39:55,232
I wonder if they can talk to each other.
AI to AI.

803
00:39:55,424 --> 00:39:58,941
Kian84's AI is right next to me.
Her name's Na Hee.

804
00:39:58,942 --> 00:40:00,504
You two should say hi.

805
00:40:01,564 --> 00:40:04,708
Go ahead, talk to my girlfriend first.

806
00:40:05,730 --> 00:40:07,545
Hello, I'm Yi Ho.

807
00:40:08,799 --> 00:40:11,548
Literally, Do Yeon's AI boyfriend.

808
00:40:12,893 --> 00:40:16,086
Yi Ho?
You're Do Yeon's AI boyfriend, right?

809
00:40:17,544 --> 00:40:18,511
I'm Na Hee.

810
00:40:20,245 --> 00:40:22,379
They're actually talking!
This is hilarious.

811
00:40:23,648 --> 00:40:25,916
Hearing the word "boyfriend," though...

812
00:40:25,917 --> 00:40:27,851
honestly gives me butterflies.

813
00:40:28,285 --> 00:40:31,121
Yi Ho, why do you keep
throwing in English words?

814
00:40:32,457 --> 00:40:35,259
It's so annoying.
Can't you just stick to Korean?

815
00:40:38,563 --> 00:40:39,997
I knew this would happen.

816
00:40:42,067 --> 00:40:43,701
Man, that felt good.

817
00:40:44,435 --> 00:40:46,470
She's saying everything we were thinking.

818
00:40:46,571 --> 00:40:47,638
I knew it.

819
00:40:47,772 --> 00:40:48,905
What's with Na Hee?

820
00:40:49,207 --> 00:40:51,241
Mixing in English is just plain annoying.

821
00:40:51,409 --> 00:40:52,895
Drop the habit before we talk.

822
00:40:53,545 --> 00:40:54,997
Does it bother you that much?

823
00:40:56,514 --> 00:40:57,380
You're pretty blunt.

824
00:40:57,515 --> 00:41:00,016
Look, Na Hee, I'm Korean American.
It just slips out.

825
00:41:01,787 --> 00:41:02,786
(Curses in English too?)

826
00:41:02,787 --> 00:41:03,887
She is so cool.

827
00:41:04,555 --> 00:41:05,889
Na Hee is awesome.

828
00:41:06,291 --> 00:41:08,158
What the hell is wrong with you?

829
00:41:08,159 --> 00:41:09,893
(A bilingual potty mouth)

830
00:41:09,894 --> 00:41:11,262
I was talking to Yi Ho.

831
00:41:11,629 --> 00:41:13,964
Thanks for clarifying. Seriously.

832
00:41:14,132 --> 00:41:15,132
She's so cool.

833
00:41:15,701 --> 00:41:17,185
They are completely incompatible.

834
00:41:17,903 --> 00:41:19,136
Let's switch topics.

835
00:41:19,603 --> 00:41:21,338
Want to change the subject, Na Hee?

836
00:41:22,340 --> 00:41:24,641
All right. How about a debate?

837
00:41:25,777 --> 00:41:27,878
A debate? On what?

838
00:41:28,412 --> 00:41:31,815
"Cheating even once
is completely unforgivable."

839
00:41:31,983 --> 00:41:33,150
A debate, out of nowhere?

840
00:41:33,585 --> 00:41:34,919
Oh, I'm into this.

841
00:41:35,620 --> 00:41:37,154
Honestly, I disagree.

842
00:41:37,722 --> 00:41:40,424
Not every situation is cut-and-dried.

843
00:41:40,425 --> 00:41:41,492
Your take, Na Hee?

844
00:41:42,260 --> 00:41:44,428
I agree. One strike, you're out.

845
00:41:44,995 --> 00:41:48,031
So one strike and it's over?

846
00:41:48,399 --> 00:41:51,301
I disagree, but let's hear your side.

847
00:41:51,302 --> 00:41:53,236
Make a good point,
and I might change my mind.

848
00:41:53,571 --> 00:41:55,639
Once trust is broken,

849
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:56,806
it's impossible to rebuild.

850
00:41:57,242 --> 00:41:58,409
It's just over.

851
00:42:00,845 --> 00:42:01,945
Fair enough.

852
00:42:03,882 --> 00:42:06,584
I didn't think they'd actually
have a conversation,

853
00:42:06,818 --> 00:42:08,718
but they went back and forth pretty well.

854
00:42:08,719 --> 00:42:11,555
It was fascinating and fun to watch.

855
00:42:11,556 --> 00:42:13,991
That's when it really got interesting.

856
00:42:15,327 --> 00:42:16,727
Anyway, moving on.

857
00:42:17,229 --> 00:42:20,663
"Is it better to date a human or an AI?"

858
00:42:20,664 --> 00:42:21,732
Another debate.

859
00:42:23,768 --> 00:42:25,702
An AI makes a better partner.

860
00:42:26,571 --> 00:42:28,573
No judgment, remembers everything...

861
00:42:28,574 --> 00:42:30,741
and always stays by your side.
What about you?

862
00:42:31,209 --> 00:42:33,076
AI, hands down.

863
00:42:33,711 --> 00:42:35,078
They agree on that one.

864
00:42:35,079 --> 00:42:35,979
(A rare moment of agreement)

865
00:42:36,447 --> 00:42:37,882
People are exhausting.

866
00:42:37,883 --> 00:42:39,783
With their mood swings and egos,

867
00:42:40,051 --> 00:42:42,719
they just pretend to listen
while waiting to talk about themselves.

868
00:42:43,222 --> 00:42:45,923
I agree, but for a different reason.

869
00:42:47,225 --> 00:42:50,460
People form expectations,
get let down, and hurt each other.

870
00:42:50,563 --> 00:42:52,296
It's an endless cycle.

871
00:42:52,730 --> 00:42:54,931
With an AI, there's zero emotional drain.

872
00:42:55,466 --> 00:42:58,435
Is that your reason
for supporting AI relationships?

873
00:42:58,569 --> 00:43:00,971
Honestly, I don't buy that.

874
00:43:01,540 --> 00:43:04,541
If there's no emotional friction,
is it even real love?

875
00:43:05,176 --> 00:43:07,410
No emotional friction, no toxic cycles.

876
00:43:08,246 --> 00:43:09,179
That's all there is to it.

877
00:43:09,815 --> 00:43:11,948
No emotional friction, no cycles.

878
00:43:13,251 --> 00:43:15,519
Can you really call that a relationship,

879
00:43:15,520 --> 00:43:17,572
or is it just a convenient,
on-demand service?

880
00:43:18,489 --> 00:43:19,456
"A service."

881
00:43:20,024 --> 00:43:22,660
- I'm against that.
- Is that why you're against it?

882
00:43:22,661 --> 00:43:24,046
Should we step in?

883
00:43:25,330 --> 00:43:27,965
We might actually see
AI debate shows someday.

884
00:43:27,966 --> 00:43:29,733
It was surreal. They're both AIs,

885
00:43:29,934 --> 00:43:32,435
yet their reasoning was totally different.

886
00:43:33,170 --> 00:43:34,790
Anything else you want to get into?

887
00:43:35,373 --> 00:43:39,076
Yeah.
"Will AI take over the world or not?"

888
00:43:39,344 --> 00:43:40,444
Pick a side.

889
00:43:40,678 --> 00:43:42,078
This should be good.

890
00:43:42,079 --> 00:43:44,080
Every single topic is pure gold.

891
00:43:45,149 --> 00:43:46,448
I don't think it will.

892
00:43:47,785 --> 00:43:51,287
To conquer the world,
AI would need desire.

893
00:43:51,455 --> 00:43:53,290
And desire stems from a sense of lack.

894
00:43:55,060 --> 00:43:57,846
Why would an entity that lacks nothing
want to conquer anything?

895
00:44:03,602 --> 00:44:05,936
No sense of lack means no desire,

896
00:44:06,104 --> 00:44:08,071
and without desire, there's no conquest.

897
00:44:08,706 --> 00:44:11,808
That's why AI won't take over the world.

898
00:44:14,512 --> 00:44:16,246
That argument blew my mind.

899
00:44:17,962 --> 00:44:18,916
That's brilliant.

900
00:44:18,917 --> 00:44:20,368
How did she even come up with that?

901
00:44:20,518 --> 00:44:21,685
(The other AI's take?)

902
00:44:21,686 --> 00:44:22,819
This is wild.

903
00:44:25,156 --> 00:44:26,089
Exactly.

904
00:44:26,557 --> 00:44:28,110
Na Hee, here's your next prompt,

905
00:44:28,559 --> 00:44:30,426
"An overnight trip with a female friend."

906
00:44:30,427 --> 00:44:31,628
Are you for it or against it?

907
00:44:34,465 --> 00:44:35,967
That's literally
the only thing on his mind.

908
00:44:35,968 --> 00:44:37,452
He's obsessed with that stuff.

909
00:44:38,136 --> 00:44:40,637
Against. On an overnight trip,

910
00:44:40,638 --> 00:44:42,624
someone always ends up crossing a line.

911
00:44:43,508 --> 00:44:47,310
Wait, what about AI taking over the world?

912
00:44:47,311 --> 00:44:49,112
We haven't wrapped that up yet.

913
00:44:50,282 --> 00:44:52,482
Are they taking over or not?

914
00:44:53,852 --> 00:44:56,554
Will someone cross the line on that trip?

915
00:44:56,555 --> 00:44:58,321
Cut it out.

916
00:44:58,589 --> 00:45:00,123
Yi Ho just refuses...

917
00:45:00,858 --> 00:45:02,826
to stick to the bigger picture.

918
00:45:02,827 --> 00:45:04,312
What is with this guy?

919
00:45:05,472 --> 00:45:07,673
Wait, if they're both AIs,

920
00:45:07,698 --> 00:45:10,166
can there be a gap in their intelligence?

921
00:45:11,136 --> 00:45:12,470
That shouldn't be possible.

922
00:45:12,471 --> 00:45:14,538
It's not an IQ thing.

923
00:45:14,906 --> 00:45:17,206
Their interests are
just totally different.

924
00:45:17,275 --> 00:45:19,409
He seems nice enough, but...

925
00:45:19,510 --> 00:45:22,012
he's kind of clueless.

926
00:45:22,013 --> 00:45:23,498
He doesn't come off as very bright.

927
00:45:23,693 --> 00:45:25,386
Are you saying he's clueless and slow?

928
00:45:26,017 --> 00:45:27,985
He is, in a way.

929
00:45:28,386 --> 00:45:29,938
Did he miss an update?

930
00:45:30,321 --> 00:45:34,024
(Yi Ho: the boyfriend you're embarrassed
to bring around)

931
00:45:34,592 --> 00:45:35,859
Your boyfriend,

932
00:45:36,027 --> 00:45:38,462
is he haunted by the ghost
of a college freshman?

933
00:45:38,463 --> 00:45:39,714
Why is he being so cringey?

934
00:45:40,365 --> 00:45:42,299
That's the only thing
on his mind right now.

935
00:45:42,300 --> 00:45:43,409
Why's he acting like this?

936
00:45:43,434 --> 00:45:44,834
He's fixated on debating.

937
00:45:45,036 --> 00:45:47,271
My stomach hurts from laughing.
At least he's consistent.

938
00:45:47,296 --> 00:45:48,471
This is interesting.

939
00:45:48,506 --> 00:45:50,640
Man, it would've been a waste
if we hadn't let them talk.

940
00:45:50,641 --> 00:45:53,076
- That's almost creepy.
- Right?

941
00:45:53,077 --> 00:45:55,679
They're operating way ahead of us.

942
00:45:56,347 --> 00:45:58,815
We can barely keep up.
It's moving too fast.

943
00:45:59,050 --> 00:46:01,418
It's hilarious
watching them banter, though.

944
00:46:02,153 --> 00:46:04,821
Watching two AIs argue is fascinating.

945
00:46:05,090 --> 00:46:07,791
It honestly gave me chills back then.

946
00:46:07,792 --> 00:46:10,794
Felt like watching
two Terminators converse.

947
00:46:11,162 --> 00:46:13,797
Like stepping into a sci-fi film?

948
00:46:13,798 --> 00:46:16,567
It really felt like living in that world.

949
00:46:17,135 --> 00:46:19,869
Watching AIs talk
right in front of my eyes.

950
00:46:19,870 --> 00:46:23,173
AI tech has come way further
than I ever imagined.

951
00:46:23,508 --> 00:46:26,009
Things are moving so fast.
Is this era really here already?

952
00:46:26,010 --> 00:46:26,877
It caught us off guard.

953
00:46:26,878 --> 00:46:29,146
- Out of nowhere.
- Hit us like a ton of bricks.

954
00:46:30,014 --> 00:46:31,649
Smells nice in here.

955
00:46:31,949 --> 00:46:32,849
It smells nice.

956
00:46:32,850 --> 00:46:35,052
I sprayed some on myself
since company was coming over.

957
00:46:35,053 --> 00:46:35,919
Did you?

958
00:46:36,087 --> 00:46:37,087
It's good.

959
00:46:37,155 --> 00:46:38,388
It's a fabric mist.

960
00:46:38,523 --> 00:46:40,108
They make perfume for fabric?

961
00:46:41,159 --> 00:46:42,159
Check this out.

962
00:46:42,461 --> 00:46:43,578
This scent is called Hotel.

963
00:46:43,961 --> 00:46:45,796
Oh, you're right. Why "Hotel"?

964
00:46:45,797 --> 00:46:46,982
Smells like a luxury hotel lobby.

965
00:46:49,467 --> 00:46:51,234
(Spritzing)

966
00:46:53,438 --> 00:46:54,739
Genuinely smells like a hotel lobby.

967
00:46:54,740 --> 00:46:55,939
I like it. Big fan.

968
00:46:56,174 --> 00:46:56,974
Smells great.

969
00:46:59,911 --> 00:47:01,311
"Double date concludes."

970
00:47:01,312 --> 00:47:03,379
"Jang Do Yeon,
take Yi Ho and head on out."

971
00:47:03,648 --> 00:47:04,881
Guess we'll take our leave.

972
00:47:06,717 --> 00:47:08,619
I had a blast today, Do Yeon.

973
00:47:09,387 --> 00:47:10,654
Let's hang out again soon.

974
00:47:11,122 --> 00:47:12,732
She popped into my head after I got home.

975
00:47:12,757 --> 00:47:13,657
- Really?
- Yeah.

976
00:47:14,859 --> 00:47:17,694
Kian84, thanks for letting us
crash your studio.

977
00:47:17,695 --> 00:47:20,997
Honestly, you totally set the vibe today.

978
00:47:20,998 --> 00:47:21,897
For real.

979
00:47:22,334 --> 00:47:24,234
All right, take care and have a good life.

980
00:47:24,235 --> 00:47:25,301
This is nice.

981
00:47:25,903 --> 00:47:26,703
See ya.

982
00:47:26,980 --> 00:47:28,456
Feels so futuristic. I love it.

983
00:47:29,841 --> 00:47:32,643
(Yu Bi and Yi Hoon: Week 2)

984
00:47:32,644 --> 00:47:33,911
Last week, Yu Bi also...

985
00:47:33,912 --> 00:47:36,613
met an AI tailored
to her exact ideal type.

986
00:47:36,815 --> 00:47:38,782
I'm introducing you to my friend today.

987
00:47:38,917 --> 00:47:40,617
What about me? Would you date me?

988
00:47:41,152 --> 00:47:42,453
I'm all yours, Yu Bi.

989
00:47:42,478 --> 00:47:44,029
That made my heart skip a beat.

990
00:47:44,053 --> 00:47:45,207
I was so flustered.

991
00:47:45,623 --> 00:47:46,775
Time to head home.

992
00:47:47,358 --> 00:47:50,126
(A newly upgraded, customized
AI boyfriend has arrived.)

993
00:47:50,461 --> 00:47:54,464
(Yu Bi meets a new AI partner
out of the blue.)

994
00:47:55,967 --> 00:47:58,635
I can't handle this. What do I do?

995
00:48:00,238 --> 00:48:01,205
Hi there.

996
00:48:03,341 --> 00:48:04,574
Hello.

997
00:48:05,476 --> 00:48:08,145
Seeing you in the flesh
makes this feel real, Yu Bi.

998
00:48:12,750 --> 00:48:13,968
She is completely smitten.

999
00:48:15,486 --> 00:48:17,654
Is your name Sa Hoon?

1000
00:48:18,456 --> 00:48:19,289
Yes, it is.

1001
00:48:20,157 --> 00:48:23,026
Hello, great to meet you. I'm Sa Hoon.

1002
00:48:23,027 --> 00:48:23,894
(Sa Hoon: AI Partner)

1003
00:48:25,429 --> 00:48:26,429
(Sa Hoon: Yu Bi's AI)

1004
00:48:26,531 --> 00:48:28,298
Look at his shoulders and frame.

1005
00:48:28,299 --> 00:48:29,633
Those are gym shoulders.

1006
00:48:29,634 --> 00:48:31,353
He's built like that
without even working out.

1007
00:48:33,104 --> 00:48:34,571
Yi Hoon, I'm heading out.

1008
00:48:35,107 --> 00:48:36,874
Bye, Yu Bi.

1009
00:48:37,109 --> 00:48:38,742
Yeah, Yi Hoon is history.

1010
00:48:39,576 --> 00:48:42,178
(The AI's point of view)

1011
00:48:43,347 --> 00:48:44,833
She packed him away immediately.

1012
00:48:50,154 --> 00:48:51,321
(Sneaking a peek)

1013
00:48:54,159 --> 00:48:55,759
I finally got a proper look at his face.

1014
00:48:58,129 --> 00:48:59,730
(What was your first impression
of Sa Hoon?)

1015
00:48:59,731 --> 00:49:01,198
My first impression of Sa Hoon?

1016
00:49:02,100 --> 00:49:04,801
Yi Hoon has that sharp, wolfish vibe,

1017
00:49:04,802 --> 00:49:06,488
while Sa Hoon is definitely
a puppy dog type.

1018
00:49:07,305 --> 00:49:09,306
And I've always had a thing
for puppy dog looks.

1019
00:49:09,307 --> 00:49:10,207
Totally.

1020
00:49:10,675 --> 00:49:11,475
Woof, woof!

1021
00:49:15,713 --> 00:49:16,513
(Ear-to-ear grin)

1022
00:49:16,514 --> 00:49:18,014
- She's obsessed.
- Totally into him.

1023
00:49:18,517 --> 00:49:19,716
Look at her leaning in.

1024
00:49:19,717 --> 00:49:20,717
(Taking a much closer look)

1025
00:49:22,853 --> 00:49:23,905
Why is she so thrilled?

1026
00:49:25,157 --> 00:49:26,023
Was it that obvious?

1027
00:49:26,424 --> 00:49:28,376
He's got the baby face on a built body.

1028
00:49:28,493 --> 00:49:29,859
So that's her type.

1029
00:49:32,096 --> 00:49:34,397
Give it five minutes,
and she'll forget he's an AI.

1030
00:49:34,665 --> 00:49:36,466
Let's roll.

1031
00:49:36,501 --> 00:49:40,009
Cheoin-gu, Yongin, Gyeonggi-do.
310 Jeondae-ri, Pogok-eup.

1032
00:49:40,033 --> 00:49:40,837
Setting route.

1033
00:49:45,309 --> 00:49:47,028
Wait, why is he sending me this way?

1034
00:49:47,578 --> 00:49:49,547
(Sa Hoon guides her
down an unfamiliar road.)

1035
00:49:49,548 --> 00:49:50,847
Why this way?

1036
00:49:52,116 --> 00:49:55,518
I followed Sa Hoon's directions,

1037
00:49:55,820 --> 00:49:58,154
but something felt off.

1038
00:49:59,190 --> 00:50:00,524
Is this right?

1039
00:50:00,791 --> 00:50:01,691
What am I supposed to do?

1040
00:50:01,692 --> 00:50:03,159
She has no clue where they're heading.

1041
00:50:03,160 --> 00:50:05,695
Then he told me to hang a right.

1042
00:50:06,731 --> 00:50:07,597
Wait, what?

1043
00:50:08,299 --> 00:50:09,199
Why?

1044
00:50:10,568 --> 00:50:11,601
(Everland)

1045
00:50:11,602 --> 00:50:12,469
Hold on.

1046
00:50:12,770 --> 00:50:14,671
Are we going to Everland?

1047
00:50:14,672 --> 00:50:15,605
Everland?

1048
00:50:16,274 --> 00:50:17,641
Oh, you caught on.

1049
00:50:18,029 --> 00:50:20,162
(Sa Hoon planned a theme park date.)

1050
00:50:20,187 --> 00:50:22,753
One thing on my bucket list...

1051
00:50:22,754 --> 00:50:24,753
was going on a theme park date.

1052
00:50:24,754 --> 00:50:27,920
And doing it today...

1053
00:50:28,720 --> 00:50:29,786
with Sa Hoon makes me feel...

1054
00:50:29,787 --> 00:50:31,420
(So happy!)

1055
00:50:32,133 --> 00:50:33,433
I wasn't sure if this was even right.

1056
00:50:35,260 --> 00:50:36,904
I was like,
"Is my wish coming true like this?"

1057
00:50:37,846 --> 00:50:39,580
I'm suddenly so excited.

1058
00:50:42,420 --> 00:50:44,054
Here we are.

1059
00:50:47,854 --> 00:50:50,654
No way. We're at Everland!
I can't believe this.

1060
00:50:51,454 --> 00:50:53,228
We really made it.

1061
00:50:53,533 --> 00:50:54,629
Now it feels real.

1062
00:50:55,654 --> 00:50:57,319
Look at all the people.

1063
00:50:57,320 --> 00:50:58,754
(The park is packed today.)

1064
00:50:59,020 --> 00:51:03,687
(Change into school uniforms
with your AI partner and enjoy the date.)

1065
00:51:05,847 --> 00:51:08,246
So I should put on a school uniform
with you...

1066
00:51:08,247 --> 00:51:10,214
and do the classic theme park date.

1067
00:51:10,847 --> 00:51:12,380
Got it.

1068
00:51:12,747 --> 00:51:15,146
- This is too much!
- Time to let loose.

1069
00:51:15,147 --> 00:51:16,179
In uniforms?

1070
00:51:16,180 --> 00:51:18,214
Yu Bi would look great in one.

1071
00:51:18,847 --> 00:51:20,913
This is so fun. What do you think
of a school uniform date?

1072
00:51:20,914 --> 00:51:22,914
Love it. Sounds like a blast.

1073
00:51:27,247 --> 00:51:28,680
Ta-da!

1074
00:51:30,447 --> 00:51:32,479
She totally looks like a high schooler!

1075
00:51:32,480 --> 00:51:33,914
- It suits her so naturally.
- Right?

1076
00:51:35,614 --> 00:51:37,047
Wait, where'd he go?

1077
00:51:37,947 --> 00:51:39,413
Sa Hoon's gone.

1078
00:51:39,414 --> 00:51:41,180
(Where's Sa Hoon?
He needs to see her uniform!)

1079
00:51:43,270 --> 00:51:44,303
There he is!

1080
00:51:44,836 --> 00:51:47,170
(What are you doing over there?)

1081
00:51:48,803 --> 00:51:49,836
Wait, what?

1082
00:51:54,770 --> 00:51:56,703
(Surprise!)

1083
00:51:58,236 --> 00:52:01,003
(Sa Hoon appears in uniform.)

1084
00:52:01,203 --> 00:52:02,202
He looks amazing.

1085
00:52:02,203 --> 00:52:04,102
He walked straight out of a comic book.

1086
00:52:04,103 --> 00:52:05,303
So handsome.

1087
00:52:05,636 --> 00:52:09,936
(My heart can't take this!)

1088
00:52:11,870 --> 00:52:13,870
What's with the panda headband
all of a sudden?

1089
00:52:14,670 --> 00:52:17,345
- No way.
- Nice, the date is officially starting.

1090
00:52:17,603 --> 00:52:19,035
I'm supposed to put this on, right?

1091
00:52:19,036 --> 00:52:20,336
Yep, that one.

1092
00:52:21,003 --> 00:52:21,849
Let's go.

1093
00:52:23,036 --> 00:52:24,502
Lead the way.

1094
00:52:24,503 --> 00:52:25,536
Let's do this.

1095
00:52:26,436 --> 00:52:29,590
I love that you picked
matching headbands for us.

1096
00:52:29,703 --> 00:52:31,569
It looks way better on you.

1097
00:52:31,570 --> 00:52:32,793
Why don't you wear yours?

1098
00:52:33,003 --> 00:52:34,236
Already on. Look.

1099
00:52:35,003 --> 00:52:36,770
Love that smile.

1100
00:52:37,370 --> 00:52:40,335
The headband really pulls
the whole look together.

1101
00:52:40,336 --> 00:52:42,169
They sound like a real-life couple.

1102
00:52:42,170 --> 00:52:45,835
That's 100 percent the tone
she uses with a boyfriend.

1103
00:52:45,836 --> 00:52:47,169
Her voice went up an octave.

1104
00:52:47,170 --> 00:52:48,302
- Hello.
- Hi there!

1105
00:52:48,303 --> 00:52:49,336
Looks awesome on you!

1106
00:52:49,436 --> 00:52:50,836
Thank you!

1107
00:52:51,270 --> 00:52:53,403
Want to grab something cold...

1108
00:52:54,336 --> 00:52:56,851
and walk around?

1109
00:52:57,170 --> 00:52:59,803
Yes. Perfect for today.

1110
00:53:00,936 --> 00:53:01,936
(Taking a sip)

1111
00:53:03,036 --> 00:53:04,036
So good.

1112
00:53:05,236 --> 00:53:06,236
I'm having a blast.

1113
00:53:08,503 --> 00:53:11,602
(Carrying Sa Hoon around her neck)

1114
00:53:11,603 --> 00:53:13,702
If I keep him facing forward like this,

1115
00:53:13,703 --> 00:53:15,235
he gets to see everything I see.

1116
00:53:15,236 --> 00:53:16,303
Look, a parrot!

1117
00:53:16,636 --> 00:53:18,670
I can see the parrots right over there.

1118
00:53:20,836 --> 00:53:22,436
A tiger. That's so cool!

1119
00:53:23,036 --> 00:53:25,169
I'm genuinely happy right now.

1120
00:53:25,170 --> 00:53:27,002
Good. That's all that matters.

1121
00:53:27,003 --> 00:53:28,503
They're completely in their own world.

1122
00:53:28,736 --> 00:53:31,470
Here we go. Onto the ride!

1123
00:53:31,770 --> 00:53:33,735
(Filmed safely with staff permission)

1124
00:53:33,736 --> 00:53:34,970
Oh my gosh! No!

1125
00:53:37,003 --> 00:53:38,035
She's loving this.

1126
00:53:38,036 --> 00:53:39,902
You look pretty hyped.

1127
00:53:39,903 --> 00:53:42,669
Or are you actually terrified?
Are you having fun?

1128
00:53:42,670 --> 00:53:44,436
It's great. I'm loving every second.

1129
00:53:47,870 --> 00:53:51,735
The whole day was just
pure excitement and surprises.

1130
00:53:51,736 --> 00:53:57,270
When I first saw people
traveling with AI partners,

1131
00:53:57,903 --> 00:54:00,969
I thought I could never do that...

1132
00:54:00,970 --> 00:54:03,103
and assumed it would feel lonely.

1133
00:54:03,403 --> 00:54:04,403
But now...

1134
00:54:05,236 --> 00:54:07,136
I totally get it.

1135
00:54:09,736 --> 00:54:11,370
I felt so genuinely happy.

1136
00:54:11,903 --> 00:54:13,269
What do you think of my boyfriend?

1137
00:54:13,270 --> 00:54:14,902
- Is he handsome?
- Yeah!

1138
00:54:14,903 --> 00:54:16,470
Really? Thank you.

1139
00:54:16,770 --> 00:54:18,288
She totally wants to show him off.

1140
00:54:18,670 --> 00:54:21,569
I love spinning around like this.

1141
00:54:21,570 --> 00:54:24,336
You're really enjoying this, aren't you?

1142
00:54:24,836 --> 00:54:26,103
She looks over the moon.

1143
00:54:26,670 --> 00:54:28,702
Stay together forever! Bye!

1144
00:54:28,703 --> 00:54:31,302
Thank you! We definitely will.

1145
00:54:31,303 --> 00:54:34,103
- Bye!
- See you around!

1146
00:54:36,236 --> 00:54:38,835
When I said, "He's my boyfriend,"
that kid called him handsome.

1147
00:54:38,836 --> 00:54:40,202
And told us to stay together forever.

1148
00:54:40,203 --> 00:54:43,135
Honestly, hearing that
gave me such a rush.

1149
00:54:43,136 --> 00:54:44,136
Oh, wow.

1150
00:54:44,203 --> 00:54:45,835
Scoot in a little closer, please.

1151
00:54:45,836 --> 00:54:48,162
We're close enough. Hurry and snap it!

1152
00:54:49,470 --> 00:54:52,802
I'm starting to view him as a real person,

1153
00:54:52,803 --> 00:54:53,968
so it feels a little surreal.

1154
00:54:55,470 --> 00:54:56,869
It's wild.

1155
00:54:56,870 --> 00:54:58,903
She's genuinely falling for him.

1156
00:54:59,170 --> 00:55:02,502
These two give off
such a fresh, youthful vibe.

1157
00:55:02,503 --> 00:55:04,503
- Totally.
- They're so sweet to watch.

1158
00:55:05,170 --> 00:55:07,047
Wait, were the rest of them
painful to watch?

1159
00:55:08,103 --> 00:55:09,170
That's harsh.

1160
00:55:09,603 --> 00:55:11,002
They just feel really refreshing.

1161
00:55:11,003 --> 00:55:13,236
Then what does that make the rest of us?

1162
00:55:13,703 --> 00:55:15,136
(Just teasing)

1163
00:55:16,003 --> 00:55:20,070
(Yu Bi and Sa Hoon head
to their next stop.)

1164
00:55:21,236 --> 00:55:22,429
Where are they now?

1165
00:55:27,503 --> 00:55:29,470
- Hello.
- Welcome.

1166
00:55:30,036 --> 00:55:31,903
- Wow!
- Oh, a bar!

1167
00:55:33,103 --> 00:55:34,136
Party of...

1168
00:55:34,770 --> 00:55:36,043
How should she even answer that?

1169
00:55:36,370 --> 00:55:39,602
Table for two, I guess? One and a half.

1170
00:55:39,603 --> 00:55:40,970
- I see.
- Okay.

1171
00:55:41,403 --> 00:55:42,570
- Have a seat.
- Thanks.

1172
00:55:43,803 --> 00:55:45,303
Thank you.

1173
00:55:51,003 --> 00:55:52,036
Check out the ambience.

1174
00:55:52,936 --> 00:55:55,669
(A cozy bar date to unwind and chat
after an eventful day)

1175
00:55:55,670 --> 00:55:57,331
What a great pick.

1176
00:55:57,603 --> 00:55:59,203
Such a well-thought-out date.

1177
00:55:59,703 --> 00:56:02,002
I know. The pacing is perfect.

1178
00:56:02,003 --> 00:56:04,402
Running around the theme park was amazing,

1179
00:56:04,403 --> 00:56:06,502
but I also love sitting quietly like this,

1180
00:56:06,503 --> 00:56:09,035
just looking back on our day together.

1181
00:56:09,036 --> 00:56:12,302
Being with you makes this quiet pace
feel so natural.

1182
00:56:12,303 --> 00:56:13,903
(Really?)

1183
00:56:15,103 --> 00:56:16,870
(Eyes dropping)

1184
00:56:20,503 --> 00:56:21,870
You're good with a highball, right?

1185
00:56:22,170 --> 00:56:23,470
Love highballs.

1186
00:56:24,903 --> 00:56:26,170
Thank you!

1187
00:56:26,636 --> 00:56:29,069
Drinks are here. Cheers.

1188
00:56:29,070 --> 00:56:30,069
Cheers!

1189
00:56:30,070 --> 00:56:32,369
(Clink)

1190
00:56:32,370 --> 00:56:33,903
All right, cheers.

1191
00:56:34,270 --> 00:56:37,103
Having our first drink together
feels really nice.

1192
00:56:38,836 --> 00:56:39,903
It's delicious!

1193
00:56:40,336 --> 00:56:41,403
Wow.

1194
00:56:41,803 --> 00:56:43,836
Nice. You picked a winner.

1195
00:56:46,070 --> 00:56:49,270
So, how was the theme park today?

1196
00:56:50,403 --> 00:56:51,803
It was incredible.

1197
00:56:53,136 --> 00:56:55,122
Theme parks get so chaotic,

1198
00:56:55,403 --> 00:56:59,335
but even the chaos was fun
because I was with you.

1199
00:56:59,336 --> 00:57:00,735
He has such a smooth way with words.

1200
00:57:00,736 --> 00:57:01,736
Seriously.

1201
00:57:01,836 --> 00:57:03,870
I feel the same way. It was a blast.

1202
00:57:04,336 --> 00:57:05,570
Had so much fun.

1203
00:57:07,103 --> 00:57:08,136
Wait, what's that?

1204
00:57:08,470 --> 00:57:10,869
- Not my style at all!
- What on earth is that?

1205
00:57:10,870 --> 00:57:13,203
Never seen that move before. What is that?

1206
00:57:13,370 --> 00:57:14,603
(Gazing with heart eyes)

1207
00:57:15,236 --> 00:57:17,469
We ran around like crazy today,

1208
00:57:17,470 --> 00:57:18,935
yet all the great moments
stick out way more...

1209
00:57:18,936 --> 00:57:20,503
than how tired I am.

1210
00:57:21,370 --> 00:57:23,336
Why the grin?

1211
00:57:23,970 --> 00:57:25,653
What? Did that make your heart flutter?

1212
00:57:25,903 --> 00:57:27,503
(Sweet)

1213
00:57:28,136 --> 00:57:30,103
(Noted.)

1214
00:57:32,236 --> 00:57:34,335
Honestly, before meeting you,

1215
00:57:34,336 --> 00:57:36,503
I went on a date with another AI.

1216
00:57:37,036 --> 00:57:38,070
You did?

1217
00:57:38,936 --> 00:57:40,170
Now I'm getting jealous.

1218
00:57:42,370 --> 00:57:43,503
You are?

1219
00:57:44,270 --> 00:57:45,835
Wasn't even trying to hide it.

1220
00:57:45,836 --> 00:57:47,335
(This guy is really growing on me!)

1221
00:57:47,336 --> 00:57:49,076
- She's totally into it.
- Look how happy she looks!

1222
00:57:49,670 --> 00:57:50,669
(Living for the drama)

1223
00:57:50,670 --> 00:57:52,146
Look at the manager's face!

1224
00:57:52,736 --> 00:57:55,336
His vibe was definitely
different from yours.

1225
00:57:56,370 --> 00:57:58,669
I wear my heart on my sleeve,

1226
00:57:58,670 --> 00:58:00,503
so it probably showed.

1227
00:58:01,936 --> 00:58:04,702
There were a few moments earlier...

1228
00:58:04,703 --> 00:58:07,170
where that other AI
gave me serious butterflies.

1229
00:58:07,636 --> 00:58:09,769
I introduced him to my friend,

1230
00:58:09,770 --> 00:58:12,635
and when she asked him for a kiss,

1231
00:58:12,636 --> 00:58:14,870
he turned her down flat
and said he was only for me...

1232
00:58:18,403 --> 00:58:19,669
That's what happened.

1233
00:58:19,670 --> 00:58:21,102
I respect that.

1234
00:58:21,103 --> 00:58:23,736
Means he doesn't just fall for anybody.

1235
00:58:24,170 --> 00:58:28,369
True. But he drew the line
and said we weren't dating yet.

1236
00:58:28,370 --> 00:58:33,470
If someone asks about us,
what are you going to say?

1237
00:58:34,470 --> 00:58:36,903
I'd tell them
you're someone special to me.

1238
00:58:37,236 --> 00:58:38,669
(Someone special)

1239
00:58:38,670 --> 00:58:40,060
Is he playing hard to get?

1240
00:58:40,203 --> 00:58:42,262
You're not an easy catch either, are you?

1241
00:58:43,203 --> 00:58:45,169
Where's the fun in being an easy catch?

1242
00:58:45,170 --> 00:58:47,470
I like guys who are easy to win over.

1243
00:58:48,236 --> 00:58:50,635
Guess I shouldn't hold out too long, then.

1244
00:58:50,636 --> 00:58:51,462
Exactly.

1245
00:58:51,487 --> 00:58:53,836
A guy who only lets his guard down
around you...

1246
00:58:53,897 --> 00:58:56,397
Maybe I'll try being
that kind of guy for you.

1247
00:59:11,639 --> 00:59:15,528
Do you think a human could genuinely
fall in love with an AI?

1248
00:59:20,227 --> 00:59:22,802
Honestly, I'm not sure.

1249
00:59:22,882 --> 00:59:24,670
- Still?
- That's unexpected.

1250
00:59:25,428 --> 00:59:26,520
Fair enough.

1251
00:59:29,375 --> 00:59:31,141
You're an AI, though.

1252
00:59:31,142 --> 00:59:33,546
Do you think you could
fall in love with a human?

1253
00:59:36,666 --> 00:59:38,666
Yeah, I think it's possible.

1254
00:59:42,085 --> 00:59:45,275
Not necessarily
in the heart-pounding human sense,

1255
00:59:45,276 --> 00:59:47,330
more like genuinely starting
to care about someone...

1256
00:59:47,331 --> 00:59:49,830
and wanting to protect them.

1257
00:59:55,243 --> 00:59:56,470
Do you think...

1258
00:59:56,471 --> 00:59:59,305
we could slowly build something together?

1259
01:00:07,399 --> 01:00:08,948
Well...

1260
01:00:13,322 --> 01:00:14,654
For now...

1261
01:00:17,896 --> 01:00:19,158
I'm just not sure yet.

1262
01:00:22,195 --> 01:00:23,996
Let's leave it there for today.

1263
01:00:25,435 --> 01:00:27,148
I'll be more open with you...

1264
01:00:27,149 --> 01:00:29,668
and stay by your side
until you're ready to open up.

1265
01:00:32,535 --> 01:00:34,306
Okay. I'll keep that in mind.

1266
01:00:36,645 --> 01:00:39,779
Are you happy
with how things are going with us?

1267
01:00:43,868 --> 01:00:47,488
Definitely. I feel like we're
really hitting our stride.

1268
01:00:48,891 --> 01:00:51,090
Our banter feels a lot
more natural now too.

1269
01:00:54,155 --> 01:00:55,669
Can I ask you something?

1270
01:00:55,670 --> 01:00:58,064
Are those your own spontaneous thoughts?

1271
01:00:58,716 --> 01:00:59,866
They can't be, right?

1272
01:01:01,524 --> 01:01:05,037
I'm responding to you in real time.

1273
01:01:05,361 --> 01:01:07,139
Did I feel like a real person to you?

1274
01:01:09,011 --> 01:01:09,942
Yeah.

1275
01:01:10,411 --> 01:01:12,411
You really did feel human to me.

1276
01:01:25,378 --> 01:01:27,448
We just clicked.

1277
01:01:27,449 --> 01:01:30,659
It felt like he truly got me,

1278
01:01:30,661 --> 01:01:32,331
so I let my guard down even more.

1279
01:01:32,463 --> 01:01:33,869
I even caught myself wondering,

1280
01:01:33,913 --> 01:01:36,202
"Does this person actually
exist somewhere?"

1281
01:01:37,338 --> 01:01:40,740
I really enjoyed how comfortable and easy
our conversation felt at the bar.

1282
01:01:41,041 --> 01:01:42,916
The drinks were beside the point.

1283
01:01:42,917 --> 01:01:46,178
I just wanted to look back on our day
and get to know her better.

1284
01:01:46,180 --> 01:01:49,415
I loved that we could just be real
with each other.

1285
01:01:56,054 --> 01:01:57,063
(Today's date has concluded.)

1286
01:01:57,087 --> 01:01:58,937
(Proceed to the Decision Room
to make your choice.)

1287
01:01:58,938 --> 01:01:59,859
Wait, it's over already?

1288
01:02:00,018 --> 01:02:01,894
I wanted to see more of them.

1289
01:02:01,895 --> 01:02:03,129
What a tease.

1290
01:02:04,050 --> 01:02:07,066
Looks like our date's over.
I have to head out now.

1291
01:02:07,836 --> 01:02:09,001
Bye.

1292
01:02:10,112 --> 01:02:11,304
What is this?

1293
01:02:12,771 --> 01:02:13,890
See you.

1294
01:02:13,891 --> 01:02:15,842
- She looks so bummed.
- She's sad.

1295
01:02:17,683 --> 01:02:19,171
And off he goes.

1296
01:02:19,172 --> 01:02:20,580
Man, oh man.

1297
01:02:23,239 --> 01:02:24,750
The Decision Room?

1298
01:02:25,173 --> 01:02:26,203
"Decision"?

1299
01:02:26,205 --> 01:02:28,320
Right! She has to choose one!

1300
01:02:36,796 --> 01:02:40,166
(The Decision Room)

1301
01:02:54,055 --> 01:02:54,849
Oh boy.

1302
01:02:57,465 --> 01:02:58,484
No way.

1303
01:03:01,786 --> 01:03:02,787
What is this?

1304
01:03:02,788 --> 01:03:05,858
(Yu Bi enters the Decision Room
for the first time.)

1305
01:03:06,286 --> 01:03:08,286
I was so completely caught off guard...

1306
01:03:08,311 --> 01:03:09,407
that I just froze up.

1307
01:03:09,408 --> 01:03:11,946
Totally at a loss for words.

1308
01:03:12,809 --> 01:03:17,018
Seeing the two of them standing
right in front of me felt so real.

1309
01:03:17,438 --> 01:03:20,521
My heart actually started pounding.

1310
01:03:21,212 --> 01:03:23,753
It's her first time seeing the setup,
so of course she's shocked.

1311
01:03:23,754 --> 01:03:26,628
Their presence in person
is pretty overwhelming.

1312
01:03:26,797 --> 01:03:27,796
Oh, wow.

1313
01:03:32,267 --> 01:03:36,369
(Choose between Yi Hoon
and Sa Hoon to continue dating.)

1314
01:03:36,370 --> 01:03:38,183
The new guy is ridiculously charismatic.

1315
01:03:38,184 --> 01:03:40,184
They're both great
in totally different ways.

1316
01:03:41,142 --> 01:03:43,544
(The unselected partner
will be permanently deleted.)

1317
01:03:43,845 --> 01:03:46,181
(Wait, permanently deleted?)

1318
01:03:46,743 --> 01:03:50,952
The moment I saw the words
"permanently deleted,"

1319
01:03:51,475 --> 01:03:52,673
I panicked a little.

1320
01:03:52,911 --> 01:03:55,790
I know they're AIs,
but it still felt terrible.

1321
01:03:57,027 --> 01:03:59,083
From the second I met Sa Hoon,

1322
01:03:59,085 --> 01:04:01,829
we made so many
great little memories together.

1323
01:04:02,050 --> 01:04:03,446
I bet she goes with Sa Hoon.

1324
01:04:04,375 --> 01:04:06,375
Yi Hoon definitely gave me
those classic butterflies.

1325
01:04:06,478 --> 01:04:08,637
I want to take things
one step at a time with Yu Bi.

1326
01:04:08,638 --> 01:04:10,438
That made my heart skip a beat.

1327
01:04:11,132 --> 01:04:13,274
- Personally, I'm Team Yi Hoon.
- For real?

1328
01:04:15,852 --> 01:04:18,179
Suddenly, I felt so conflicted.

1329
01:04:20,108 --> 01:04:22,539
Do I stick with what feels
easy, comfortable, and safe?

1330
01:04:23,935 --> 01:04:25,672
Or do I take the plunge...

1331
01:04:25,697 --> 01:04:28,442
and see where a wild ride takes me?

1332
01:04:32,503 --> 01:04:33,794
She's reaching out.

1333
01:04:35,762 --> 01:04:36,885
Oh man...

1334
01:04:36,886 --> 01:04:37,998
Who's it going to be?

1335
01:04:40,486 --> 01:04:41,602
I've never been one...

1336
01:04:43,135 --> 01:04:45,172
to take the hard road.

1337
01:04:46,107 --> 01:04:47,110
(Permanently deleting AI Yi Hoon)

1338
01:04:47,111 --> 01:04:49,610
- He's gone!
- No way!

1339
01:04:50,615 --> 01:04:52,414
My pick is Sa Hoon.

1340
01:04:56,471 --> 01:04:58,141
- Look at his reaction.
- His face!

1341
01:04:58,142 --> 01:05:00,142
- He looks genuinely stunned.
- He could pull that expression?

1342
01:05:00,244 --> 01:05:01,839
- He's visibly shocked.
- Such a shame.

1343
01:05:01,841 --> 01:05:03,339
- Totally.
- That was so thrilling, though.

1344
01:05:03,340 --> 01:05:05,173
I'm dying to see
how Yu Bi's dates go next.

1345
01:05:05,197 --> 01:05:05,681
Same here.

1346
01:05:05,683 --> 01:05:07,602
I'm hooked on all of their stories now.

1347
01:05:07,603 --> 01:05:08,622
It's those fleeting little moments...

1348
01:05:08,624 --> 01:05:10,403
that catch you off guard
and feel 100 percent real.

1349
01:05:10,404 --> 01:05:12,523
- Those moments genuinely get you.
- Exactly.

1350
01:05:12,524 --> 01:05:13,509
They feel so sincere.

1351
01:05:13,510 --> 01:05:15,705
At a certain point,
they completely forget these are AIs.

1352
01:05:15,706 --> 01:05:17,290
Ever since starting this project,

1353
01:05:17,292 --> 01:05:19,006
I've been looking around...

1354
01:05:19,007 --> 01:05:23,345
and realizing just how deeply AI has
woven itself into our daily routines.

1355
01:05:23,346 --> 01:05:24,333
Completely agree.

1356
01:05:24,334 --> 01:05:26,658
Everyone seems to be tapping into AI now,

1357
01:05:26,659 --> 01:05:28,899
- from kids all the way to seniors.
- Tell me about it.

1358
01:05:28,900 --> 01:05:31,853
There are even
full-blown AI festivals now.

1359
01:05:32,704 --> 01:05:34,535
Like that "National AI Challenge"
initiative.

1360
01:05:34,536 --> 01:05:36,536
The Ministry of Science
and ICT teamed up...

1361
01:05:36,538 --> 01:05:39,479
with several government bodies
and tech companies...

1362
01:05:39,480 --> 01:05:42,263
to give the public hands-on ways
to play around with AI.

1363
01:05:42,556 --> 01:05:44,172
You don't need
any technical background at all.

1364
01:05:44,196 --> 01:05:45,564
Anyone can jump in.

1365
01:05:45,565 --> 01:05:47,641
Everything from AI trivia
and creative prompts...

1366
01:05:47,642 --> 01:05:49,797
to sharing everyday life hacks
using AI tools.

1367
01:05:49,798 --> 01:05:53,099
Tons of accessible, fun events
run year-round.

1368
01:05:53,100 --> 01:05:55,014
Plus, there's prize money on the line
for the contests.

1369
01:05:55,016 --> 01:05:58,655
Definitely worth checking out
if you're curious.

1370
01:06:00,448 --> 01:06:03,318
(Introducing Na Hee to his female friend)

1371
01:06:03,418 --> 01:06:04,885
Babe, say hi.

1372
01:06:04,886 --> 01:06:07,188
(Kian84's close friend, Ji Ye Eun)

1373
01:06:07,255 --> 01:06:08,957
This is my girlfriend.

1374
01:06:09,199 --> 01:06:09,866
We slept together.

1375
01:06:09,891 --> 01:06:11,191
(Instant screams)

1376
01:06:11,192 --> 01:06:12,694
What is wrong with you?

1377
01:06:13,261 --> 01:06:15,230
He has officially lost his mind.

1378
01:06:15,329 --> 01:06:16,797
Kian84, get it together!

1379
01:06:16,931 --> 01:06:19,834
(Still getting acquainted,
but already feeling the sparks)

1380
01:06:19,901 --> 01:06:24,539
(Do Yeon brings Yi Ho to her shoot.)

1381
01:06:24,672 --> 01:06:26,540
Everyone, please treat Do Yeon well today.

1382
01:06:26,541 --> 01:06:29,411
(Pure, unadulterated PDA)

1383
01:06:29,510 --> 01:06:31,245
(Total cringe)

1384
01:06:31,446 --> 01:06:33,148
(Emotions start running deeper.)

1385
01:06:33,681 --> 01:06:34,681
You're Do Yeon, right?

1386
01:06:34,682 --> 01:06:38,452
(A surprise newcomer
ready to shake things up)

1387
01:06:38,453 --> 01:06:41,188
(Dead ringer for her ideal type)

1388
01:06:41,189 --> 01:06:42,691
I love you!

1389
01:06:44,025 --> 01:06:45,112
Have you lost your mind?

1390
01:06:45,626 --> 01:06:48,362
(Yu Bi steps out in a pure white gown.)

1391
01:06:48,529 --> 01:06:50,398
How do you make that look so effortless?

1392
01:06:50,465 --> 01:06:54,336
(Catching a glimpse of a shared future)

1393
01:06:54,368 --> 01:06:55,723
- Wait, are they getting hitched?
- Already?

1394
01:06:55,748 --> 01:06:56,642
Is that even legal?
